{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cc19","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b0ab-f92f-74d3-a245-61ad42401b4b"},"sequence":1127,"recorded_at":1780531400002249,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"8ab0c8df-167f-48db-b83c-f756aeede0a9","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"8ab0c8df-167f-48db-b83c-f756aeede0a9","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"8ab0c8df-167f-48db-b83c-f756aeede0a9"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b0b0-1f83-74b0-8699-05a22f597fb6"},"task_id":"01a0b0b0-1f83-74b0-8699-05a22f597fb6","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b0b0-1f83-74b0-8699-05a22f597fb6","chunk":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(1061 line(s) above)\n1062|### 4.C Lifecycle and operations\n1063|\n1064|Terminal Instance state is exactly <code>absent</code>, <code>creating</code>,\n1065|<code>parked</code>, <code>active</code>, <code>quiescing</code>,\n1066|<code>stopped</code>, <code>stale_fenced</code>, or <code>unavailable</code>.\n1067|This describes local hosting only; it is not a second ownership state machine.\n1068|\n1069|Every mutating request carries operation, Session, Terminal Instance and\n1070|idempotency IDs; exact backend ID/version/generation; deadline; and an expiring\n1071|AX authorization with winning lease ID/epoch. Results repeat those identities,\n1072|before/after state, side effects, evidence IDs, and one retry disposition:\n1073|<code>replay_same</code>, <code>status_first</code>,\n1074|<code>new_authorization</code>, or <code>required_operator_action</code>.\n1075|Authorization and generation are rechecked immediately before each side effect.\n1076|A deadline cancels waiting, not a committed effect.\n1077|\n1078|The closed <dfn>TerminalInstanceState</dfn> enum is the eight-state registry in\n1079|the first paragraph of this subsection. The closed\n1080|<dfn>TerminalBackendSideEffect</dfn> enum is exactly\n1081|<code>binding_persisted|wrapper_started|attach_client_created|input_closed|safe_boundary_observed|graceful_stop_requested|process_closed|backend_store_closed|stale_incarnation_terminated|wrapper_restored</code>.\n1082|The closed <dfn>PresentationTransport</dfn> enum is\n1083|<code>local_only|trusted_private_mesh|third_party_relay</code>. The closed\n1084|<dfn>ProviderProofKind</dfn> enum is\n1085|<code>provider_quiescence|provider_process_exit|ax_checkpoint_boundary</code>.\n1086|The closed <dfn>TerminalStatusLastEffect</dfn> enum is exactly\n1087|TerminalBackendSideEffect.\n1088|\n1089|<code>creating</code> is entered only by <code>create</code> after its durable\n1090|idempotency receipt and before its first listed side effect. An error before a\n1091|side effect restores the source state. An error after an effect whose result\n1092|cannot be proven moves the local observation to <code>unavailable</code> with\n1093|<code>status_first</code>; it MUST NOT claim <code>absent</code>. No operation\n1094|other than <code>quiesce-input</code> enters <code>quiescing</code>, and no\n1095|backend operation enters <code>stale_fenced</code>: AX fencing observation does.\n1096|\n1097|<dfn>AXAuthorization</dfn> is a closed object containing exactly\n1098|<code>lease_id:UUIDv4</code>, <code>lease_epoch:uint53[1..9007199254740991]</code>,\n1099|<code>holder_host_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1100|<code>authorization_kind:create|control|force_stale|restore</code>,\n1101|<code>issued_at:timestamp</code>, <code>expires_at:timestamp</code>, and\n1102|<code>authorization_evidence_id:digest</code>. Expiry is strictly after issue;\n1103|the lease tuple MUST equal the current winning AX lease at every side effect.\n1104|\n1105|<dfn>AttachAuthorization</dfn> is a closed, ownership-neutral AX policy object\n1106|containing exactly <code>policy_evidence_id:digest</code>,\n1107|<code>authorizing_host_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1108|<code>transport:PresentationTransport</code>,\n1109|<code>input_authorized:boolean</code>, <code>issued_at:timestamp</code>, and\n1110|<code>expires_at:timestamp</code>. Expiry is strictly after issue. It authorizes\n1111|only the named presentation transport and input boolean; it contains no lease\n1112|and cannot acquire, renew, or transfer ownership.\n1113|\n1114|<dfn>MutationContext</dfn> is a closed object containing exactly\n1115|<code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>session_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1116|<code>terminal_instance_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1117|<code>terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id</code>,\n1118|<code>implementation_version:semver</code>, <code>protocol_version:semver</code>,\n1119|<code>backend_generation:string[1..256]</code>,\n1120|<code>idempotency_key:string[1..256]</code>, <code>deadline_at:timestamp</code>,\n1121|and <code>authorization:AXAuthorization</code>. The key is the canonical UTF-8\n1122|encoding specified per operation below; it is not caller-chosen free text.\n1123|\n1124|<dfn>MutationResult</dfn> is a closed object containing exactly\n1125|<code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>session_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1126|<code>terminal_instance_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1127|<code>terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id</code>,\n1128|<code>implementation_version:semver</code>, <code>protocol_version:semver</code>,\n1129|<code>backend_generation:string[1..256]</code>,\n1130|<code>before_state:TerminalInstanceState</code>,\n1131|<code>after_state:TerminalInstanceState</code>,\n1132|<code>side_effects:sorted-unique TerminalBackendSideEffect[0..10]</code>,\n1133|<code>evidence_ids:sorted-unique digest[0..256]</code>, and\n1134|<code>retry_disposition:replay_same|status_first|new_authorization|required_operator_action</code>.\n1135|Every repeated identity MUST equal the request context.\n1136|\n1137|The ten operation request and success bodies are closed objects containing\n1138|exactly the listed members. <code>Entrypoint</code> is the closed object\n1139|<code>{argv:string[3]}</code>, and its three values MUST be literal\n1140|<code>ax</code>, literal <code>pane</code>, and the canonical request Session\n1141|UUIDv7 string. <code>attach_descriptor</code> is a sensitive opaque\n1142|<code>string[1..4096]</code> usable only on the responding host and MUST NOT be\n1143|persisted or replicated.\n1144|\n1145|| Operation | Exact body input | Exact success result |\n1146|| --- | --- | --- |\n1147|| <code>manifest</code> | <code>{deadline_at:timestamp}</code> | <code>{manifest:TerminalBackendManifest}</code> |\n1148|| <code>probe</code> | <code>{platform:macos\\|linux\\|wsl2\\|windows,os_version:string[1..256],requested_capabilities:sorted-unique TerminalBackendCapability[0..16],deadline_at:timestamp}</code> | <code>{probe:TerminalBackendProbe,evidence:sorted-by-evidence_id unique CapabilityEvidence[0..256]}</code> |\n1149|| <code>create</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,binding:TerminalInstanceBinding,bootstrap_operation_id:UUIDv7,entrypoint:Entrypoint,presentation_transport:PresentationTransport,interactive:boolean}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,binding:TerminalInstanceBinding,attach_descriptor:string[1..4096]\\|null}</code> |\n1150|| <code>attach</code> | <code>{session_id:UUIDv7,terminal_instance_id:UUIDv7,terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id,implementation_version:semver,protocol_version:semver,backend_generation:string[1..256],client_id:UUIDv7,transport:PresentationTransport,input_authorized:boolean,deadline_at:timestamp,authorization:AttachAuthorization}</code> | <code>{client_mirror_id:UUIDv7,attach_descriptor:string[1..4096],input_authorized:boolean,evidence_ids:sorted-unique digest[1..256]}</code> |\n1151|| <code>status</code> | <code>{session_id:UUIDv7,terminal_instance_id:UUIDv7\\|null,terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id,implementation_version:semver,protocol_version:semver,backend_generation:string[1..256]\\|null,include_provider_observation:boolean,deadline_at:timestamp}</code> | <code>{state:TerminalInstanceState,identity_match:boolean,wrapper_present:boolean,provider_present:boolean\\|null,attachable:boolean,last_operation_id:UUIDv7\\|null,last_effect:TerminalStatusLastEffect\\|null,evidence_ids:sorted-unique digest[0..256]}</code> |\n1152|| <code>quiesce-input</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,quiescence_generation:UUIDv7}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,quiescence_generation:UUIDv7,input_closed_at:timestamp}</code> |\n1153|| <code>wait-safe-boundary</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,quiescence_generation:UUIDv7,provider_proof_kind:ProviderProofKind,timeout_ms:uint53[1..3600000]}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,safe_boundary_evidence_id:digest,observed_at:timestamp}</code> |\n1154|| <code>request-stop</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,safe_boundary_evidence_id:digest,graceful_timeout_ms:uint53[1..3600000]}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,process_closed:true,store_closed:true}</code> |\n1155|| <code>terminate-stale</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,stale_lease_id:UUIDv4,stale_epoch:uint53[1..9007199254740991],diagnostic_evidence_id:digest}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,target_incarnation_closed:true}</code> |\n1156|| <code>restore</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,prior_binding_id:digest,checkpoint_id:digest,bootstrap_operation_id:UUIDv7}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,binding:TerminalInstanceBinding,restored_parked:true}</code> |\n1157|\n1158|For <code>status</code>, <code>terminal_instance_id</code> and\n1159|<code>backend_generation</code> are either both null (Session-scoped lookup) or\n1160|both non-null (exact-instance lookup). A successful exact-instance result sets\n1161|<code>identity_match</code> true only when Session, instance, backend,\n1162|implementation, protocol, and generation all match. A non-match sets\n1163|<code>identity_match:false</code>, <code>state:absent</code>,\n1164|<code>wrapper_present:false</code>, <code>provider_present:null</code>,\n1165|<code>attachable:false</code>, and both last fields null; it does not authorize\n1166|fallback. <code>provider_present</code> is null unless provider observation was\n1167|requested and evidenced. <code>attachable</code> is true only in\n1168|<code>parked|active</code> with a currently evidenced matching attach\n1169|capability. In <code>attach</code>, the result input boolean MUST equal both the\n1170|request and AttachAuthorization; <code>attach_descriptor</code> in\n1171|<code>create</code> is non-null exactly when <code>interactive</code> is true.\n1172|\n1173|The following table is the exact transition, authorization, idempotency,\n1174|deadline/recovery, evidence, capability, and Structured Error 1.3 mapping.\n1175|An error not listed for an operation MUST NOT be emitted by the backend for a\n1176|syntactically valid request; AX-local parsing may additionally emit\n1177|<code>terminal_backend_protocol_error</code>. <code>same</code> means no state\n1178|transition and no side effect.\n1179|\n1180|| Operation | Allowed source → success state; exact side effects | Authorization and idempotency key | Deadline/lost-result recovery and required evidence | Capability dependencies | Allowed error codes |\n1181|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n1182|| <code>manifest</code> | no Terminal Instance source or target; none | none; byte-stable by executable/implementation digest | <code>deadline_at</code> closes adapter; retry request; Manifest ID is evidence | none | <code>terminal_backend_protocol_incompatible</code>, <code>terminal_backend_protocol_error</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1183|| <code>probe</code> | no Terminal Instance source or target; none | trusted implementation; key is request ID | <code>deadline_at</code> closes adapter; retry with a new request ID; Probe plus evidence for every true claim | none | <code>terminal_backend_untrusted</code>, <code>terminal_backend_manifest_probe_mismatch</code>, <code>terminal_backend_implementation_drift</code>, <code>terminal_backend_protocol_error</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1184|| <code>create</code> | <code>absent|stopped</code> → <code>active</code> when interactive, otherwise <code>parked</code>; <code>binding_persisted,wrapper_started</code> and optionally <code>attach_client_created</code> | <code>create</code>; UTF-8 <code>session_id + \"/\" + bootstrap_operation_id</code> | persist receipt before <code>wrapper_started</code>; identical retry replays it; uncertainty requires <code>status</code>; binding plus capability/credential evidence | <code>headless_creation</code> when non-interactive; <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> when provider credentials are required | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unavailable</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1185|| <code>attach</code> | <code>parked</code> → <code>active</code> or <code>active</code> → <code>active</code>; <code>attach_client_created</code> | valid unexpired AttachAuthorization equal to request transport/input; UTF-8 <code>terminal_instance_id + \"/\" + client_id</code> | timeout creates no authorized input unless the durable client receipt says so; retry same client ID; attach-policy/capability evidence | matching <code>local_attach|remote_attach|web_attach</code>; <code>multi_attach</code> for overlap; <code>multiple_input_clients</code> plus AX policy for concurrent input | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unavailable</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1186|| <code>status</code> | <code>absent|creating|parked|active|quiescing|stopped|stale_fenced|unavailable</code> → same state; none | none; key is full queried identity tuple | timeout/read failure is unknown, never absent; retry query; status evidence IDs only | <code>provider_process_observation</code> exactly when provider observation requested | <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unavailable</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1187|| <code>quiesce-input</code> | <code>active|parked</code> → <code>quiescing</code>; <code>input_closed</code> | <code>control</code>; UTF-8 <code>terminal_instance_id + \"/quiesce/\" + quiescence_generation</code> | receipt precedes input closure; identical retry replays; uncertainty uses <code>status</code>; evidence binds closure time/generation | <code>input_quiescence</code> | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1188|| <code>wait-safe-boundary</code> | <code>quiescing</code> → <code>quiescing</code>; <code>safe_boundary_observed</code> | <code>control</code>; UTF-8 <code>terminal_instance_id + \"/boundary/\" + quiescence_generation + \"/\" + provider_proof_kind</code> | lesser of request deadline and timeout; identical retry returns the same proof; no proof on timeout; safe-boundary evidence | <code>safe_boundary_observation</code>; also <code>provider_process_observation</code> for provider proof kinds | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>quiesce_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1189|| <code>request-stop</code> | <code>quiescing</code> → <code>stopped</code>; <code>graceful_stop_requested,process_closed,backend_store_closed</code> | <code>control</code>; UTF-8 <code>terminal_instance_id + \"/stop/\" + safe_boundary_evidence_id</code> | lesser deadline/timeout; lost result requires <code>status</code>, then same-key retry only if not closed; boundary and closure evidence | <code>graceful_stop</code> | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>stop_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1190|| <code>terminate-stale</code> | <code>stale_fenced|unavailable</code> → <code>stopped</code>; <code>stale_incarnation_terminated,process_closed</code> | <code>force_stale</code>; UTF-8 <code>terminal_instance_id + \"/terminate/\" + stale_lease_id + \"/\" + decimal(stale_epoch)</code> | deadline may leave uncertain closure; use <code>status</code> before same-key retry; diagnostic, fencing, and closure evidence | <code>stale_process_termination</code> and <code>provider_process_observation</code> | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1191|| <code>restore</code> | <code>absent|stopped|unavailable</code> → <code>parked</code>; <code>binding_persisted,wrapper_restored</code> | <code>restore</code>; UTF-8 <code>session_id + \"/\" + bootstrap_operation_id</code> | persist receipt before restore; identical retry replays; uncertainty uses <code>status</code>; prior binding, Checkpoint, new binding, capability/credential evidence | <code>reboot_restoration</code>; <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> when credentials are required | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_restore_mismatch</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unavailable</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1192|\n1193|Create is idempotent on <code>(session_id, bootstrap_operation_id)</code> across\n1194|controller crash and lost result. AX and backend durably bind the pair before\n1195|the first child side effect. Identical retry returns the one result/instance;\n1196|a changed operation in the bootstrap window is <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>.\n1197|Only a successful status read proves absence. Attach is ownership-observational\n1198|for current-owner resume, local/remote/web, reconnect, and multi-attach.\n1199|\n1200|### 4.D Closed capabilities and evidence\n1201|\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cc1b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b0ab-f92f-74d3-a245-61ad42401b4b"},"sequence":1128,"recorded_at":1780531400002251,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"8ab0c8df-167f-48db-b83c-f756aeede0a9","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"8ab0c8df-167f-48db-b83c-f756aeede0a9","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"8ab0c8df-167f-48db-b83c-f756aeede0a9"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b0b0-1f83-74b0-8699-05a22f597fb6"},"task_id":"01a0b0b0-1f83-74b0-8699-05a22f597fb6","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"01a0b0b0-1f83-74b0-8699-05a22f597fb6"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cc1d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b0ab-f92f-74d3-a245-61ad42401b4b"},"sequence":1129,"recorded_at":1780531400002253,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"8ab0c8df-167f-48db-b83c-f756aeede0a9","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"8ab0c8df-167f-48db-b83c-f756aeede0a9","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"8ab0c8df-167f-48db-b83c-f756aeede0a9"},"call_id":"call_01a0b0b0192076d492d6511b1c96eb8f","text":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(1061 line(s) above)\n1062|### 4.C Lifecycle and operations\n1063|\n1064|Terminal Instance state is exactly <code>absent</code>, <code>creating</code>,\n1065|<code>parked</code>, <code>active</code>, <code>quiescing</code>,\n1066|<code>stopped</code>, <code>stale_fenced</code>, or <code>unavailable</code>.\n1067|This describes local hosting only; it is not a second ownership state machine.\n1068|\n1069|Every mutating request carries operation, Session, Terminal Instance and\n1070|idempotency IDs; exact backend ID/version/generation; deadline; and an expiring\n1071|AX authorization with winning lease ID/epoch. Results repeat those identities,\n1072|before/after state, side effects, evidence IDs, and one retry disposition:\n1073|<code>replay_same</code>, <code>status_first</code>,\n1074|<code>new_authorization</code>, or <code>required_operator_action</code>.\n1075|Authorization and generation are rechecked immediately before each side effect.\n1076|A deadline cancels waiting, not a committed effect.\n1077|\n1078|The closed <dfn>TerminalInstanceState</dfn> enum is the eight-state registry in\n1079|the first paragraph of this subsection. The closed\n1080|<dfn>TerminalBackendSideEffect</dfn> enum is exactly\n1081|<code>binding_persisted|wrapper_started|attach_client_created|input_closed|safe_boundary_observed|graceful_stop_requested|process_closed|backend_store_closed|stale_incarnation_terminated|wrapper_restored</code>.\n1082|The closed <dfn>PresentationTransport</dfn> enum is\n1083|<code>local_only|trusted_private_mesh|third_party_relay</code>. The closed\n1084|<dfn>ProviderProofKind</dfn> enum is\n1085|<code>provider_quiescence|provider_process_exit|ax_checkpoint_boundary</code>.\n1086|The closed <dfn>TerminalStatusLastEffect</dfn> enum is exactly\n1087|TerminalBackendSideEffect.\n1088|\n1089|<code>creating</code> is entered only by <code>create</code> after its durable\n1090|idempotency receipt and before its first listed side effect. An error before a\n1091|side effect restores the source state. An error after an effect whose result\n1092|cannot be proven moves the local observation to <code>unavailable</code> with\n1093|<code>status_first</code>; it MUST NOT claim <code>absent</code>. No operation\n1094|other than <code>quiesce-input</code> enters <code>quiescing</code>, and no\n1095|backend operation enters <code>stale_fenced</code>: AX fencing observation does.\n1096|\n1097|<dfn>AXAuthorization</dfn> is a closed object containing exactly\n1098|<code>lease_id:UUIDv4</code>, <code>lease_epoch:uint53[1..9007199254740991]</code>,\n1099|<code>holder_host_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1100|<code>authorization_kind:create|control|force_stale|restore</code>,\n1101|<code>issued_at:timestamp</code>, <code>expires_at:timestamp</code>, and\n1102|<code>authorization_evidence_id:digest</code>. Expiry is strictly after issue;\n1103|the lease tuple MUST equal the current winning AX lease at every side effect.\n1104|\n1105|<dfn>AttachAuthorization</dfn> is a closed, ownership-neutral AX policy object\n1106|containing exactly <code>policy_evidence_id:digest</code>,\n1107|<code>authorizing_host_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1108|<code>transport:PresentationTransport</code>,\n1109|<code>input_authorized:boolean</code>, <code>issued_at:timestamp</code>, and\n1110|<code>expires_at:timestamp</code>. Expiry is strictly after issue. It authorizes\n1111|only the named presentation transport and input boolean; it contains no lease\n1112|and cannot acquire, renew, or transfer ownership.\n1113|\n1114|<dfn>MutationContext</dfn> is a closed object containing exactly\n1115|<code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>session_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1116|<code>terminal_instance_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1117|<code>terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id</code>,\n1118|<code>implementation_version:semver</code>, <code>protocol_version:semver</code>,\n1119|<code>backend_generation:string[1..256]</code>,\n1120|<code>idempotency_key:string[1..256]</code>, <code>deadline_at:timestamp</code>,\n1121|and <code>authorization:AXAuthorization</code>. The key is the canonical UTF-8\n1122|encoding specified per operation below; it is not caller-chosen free text.\n1123|\n1124|<dfn>MutationResult</dfn> is a closed object containing exactly\n1125|<code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>session_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1126|<code>terminal_instance_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1127|<code>terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id</code>,\n1128|<code>implementation_version:semver</code>, <code>protocol_version:semver</code>,\n1129|<code>backend_generation:string[1..256]</code>,\n1130|<code>before_state:TerminalInstanceState</code>,\n1131|<code>after_state:TerminalInstanceState</code>,\n1132|<code>side_effects:sorted-unique TerminalBackendSideEffect[0..10]</code>,\n1133|<code>evidence_ids:sorted-unique digest[0..256]</code>, and\n1134|<code>retry_disposition:replay_same|status_first|new_authorization|required_operator_action</code>.\n1135|Every repeated identity MUST equal the request context.\n1136|\n1137|The ten operation request and success bodies are closed objects containing\n1138|exactly the listed members. <code>Entrypoint</code> is the closed object\n1139|<code>{argv:string[3]}</code>, and its three values MUST be literal\n1140|<code>ax</code>, literal <code>pane</code>, and the canonical request Session\n1141|UUIDv7 string. <code>attach_descriptor</code> is a sensitive opaque\n1142|<code>string[1..4096]</code> usable only on the responding host and MUST NOT be\n1143|persisted or replicated.\n1144|\n1145|| Operation | Exact body input | Exact success result |\n1146|| --- | --- | --- |\n1147|| <code>manifest</code> | <code>{deadline_at:timestamp}</code> | <code>{manifest:TerminalBackendManifest}</code> |\n1148|| <code>probe</code> | <code>{platform:macos\\|linux\\|wsl2\\|windows,os_version:string[1..256],requested_capabilities:sorted-unique TerminalBackendCapability[0..16],deadline_at:timestamp}</code> | <code>{probe:TerminalBackendProbe,evidence:sorted-by-evidence_id unique CapabilityEvidence[0..256]}</code> |\n1149|| <code>create</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,binding:TerminalInstanceBinding,bootstrap_operation_id:UUIDv7,entrypoint:Entrypoint,presentation_transport:PresentationTransport,interactive:boolean}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,binding:TerminalInstanceBinding,attach_descriptor:string[1..4096]\\|null}</code> |\n1150|| <code>attach</code> | <code>{session_id:UUIDv7,terminal_instance_id:UUIDv7,terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id,implementation_version:semver,protocol_version:semver,backend_generation:string[1..256],client_id:UUIDv7,transport:PresentationTransport,input_authorized:boolean,deadline_at:timestamp,authorization:AttachAuthorization}</code> | <code>{client_mirror_id:UUIDv7,attach_descriptor:string[1..4096],input_authorized:boolean,evidence_ids:sorted-unique digest[1..256]}</code> |\n1151|| <code>status</code> | <code>{session_id:UUIDv7,terminal_instance_id:UUIDv7\\|null,terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id,implementation_version:semver,protocol_version:semver,backend_generation:string[1..256]\\|null,include_provider_observation:boolean,deadline_at:timestamp}</code> | <code>{state:TerminalInstanceState,identity_match:boolean,wrapper_present:boolean,provider_present:boolean\\|null,attachable:boolean,last_operation_id:UUIDv7\\|null,last_effect:TerminalStatusLastEffect\\|null,evidence_ids:sorted-unique digest[0..256]}</code> |\n1152|| <code>quiesce-input</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,quiescence_generation:UUIDv7}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,quiescence_generation:UUIDv7,input_closed_at:timestamp}</code> |\n1153|| <code>wait-safe-boundary</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,quiescence_generation:UUIDv7,provider_proof_kind:ProviderProofKind,timeout_ms:uint53[1..3600000]}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,safe_boundary_evidence_id:digest,observed_at:timestamp}</code> |\n1154|| <code>request-stop</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,safe_boundary_evidence_id:digest,graceful_timeout_ms:uint53[1..3600000]}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,process_closed:true,store_closed:true}</code> |\n1155|| <code>terminate-stale</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,stale_lease_id:UUIDv4,stale_epoch:uint53[1..9007199254740991],diagnostic_evidence_id:digest}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,target_incarnation_closed:true}</code> |\n1156|| <code>restore</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,prior_binding_id:digest,checkpoint_id:digest,bootstrap_operation_id:UUIDv7}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,binding:TerminalInstanceBinding,restored_parked:true}</code> |\n1157|\n1158|For <code>status</code>, <code>terminal_instance_id</code> and\n1159|<code>backend_generation</code> are either both null (Session-scoped lookup) or\n1160|both non-null (exact-instance lookup). A successful exact-instance result sets\n1161|<code>identity_match</code> true only when Session, instance, backend,\n1162|implementation, protocol, and generation all match. A non-match sets\n1163|<code>identity_match:false</code>, <code>state:absent</code>,\n1164|<code>wrapper_present:false</code>, <code>provider_present:null</code>,\n1165|<code>attachable:false</code>, and both last fields null; it does not authorize\n1166|fallback. <code>provider_present</code> is null unless provider observation was\n1167|requested and evidenced. <code>attachable</code> is true only in\n1168|<code>parked|active</code> with a currently evidenced matching attach\n1169|capability. In <code>attach</code>, the result input boolean MUST equal both the\n1170|request and AttachAuthorization; <code>attach_descriptor</code> in\n1171|<code>create</code> is non-null exactly when <code>interactive</code> is true.\n1172|\n1173|The following table is the exact transition, authorization, idempotency,\n1174|deadline/recovery, evidence, capability, and Structured Error 1.3 mapping.\n1175|An error not listed for an operation MUST NOT be emitted by the backend for a\n1176|syntactically valid request; AX-local parsing may additionally emit\n1177|<code>terminal_backend_protocol_error</code>. <code>same</code> means no state\n1178|transition and no side effect.\n1179|\n1180|| Operation | Allowed source → success state; exact side effects | Authorization and idempotency key | Deadline/lost-result recovery and required evidence | Capability dependencies | Allowed error codes |\n1181|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n1182|| <code>manifest</code> | no Terminal Instance source or target; none | none; byte-stable by executable/implementation digest | <code>deadline_at</code> closes adapter; retry request; Manifest ID is evidence | none | <code>terminal_backend_protocol_incompatible</code>, <code>terminal_backend_protocol_error</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1183|| <code>probe</code> | no Terminal Instance source or target; none | trusted implementation; key is request ID | <code>deadline_at</code> closes adapter; retry with a new request ID; Probe plus evidence for every true claim | none | <code>terminal_backend_untrusted</code>, <code>terminal_backend_manifest_probe_mismatch</code>, <code>terminal_backend_implementation_drift</code>, <code>terminal_backend_protocol_error</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1184|| <code>create</code> | <code>absent|stopped</code> → <code>active</code> when interactive, otherwise <code>parked</code>; <code>binding_persisted,wrapper_started</code> and optionally <code>attach_client_created</code> | <code>create</code>; UTF-8 <code>session_id + \"/\" + bootstrap_operation_id</code> | persist receipt before <code>wrapper_started</code>; identical retry replays it; uncertainty requires <code>status</code>; binding plus capability/credential evidence | <code>headless_creation</code> when non-interactive; <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> when provider credentials are required | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unavailable</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1185|| <code>attach</code> | <code>parked</code> → <code>active</code> or <code>active</code> → <code>active</code>; <code>attach_client_created</code> | valid unexpired AttachAuthorization equal to request transport/input; UTF-8 <code>terminal_instance_id + \"/\" + client_id</code> | timeout creates no authorized input unless the durable client receipt says so; retry same client ID; attach-policy/capability evidence | matching <code>local_attach|remote_attach|web_attach</code>; <code>multi_attach</code> for overlap; <code>multiple_input_clients</code> plus AX policy for concurrent input | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unavailable</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1186|| <code>status</code> | <code>absent|creating|parked|active|quiescing|stopped|stale_fenced|unavailable</code> → same state; none | none; key is full queried identity tuple | timeout/read failure is unknown, never absent; retry query; status evidence IDs only | <code>provider_process_observation</code> exactly when provider observation requested | <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unavailable</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1187|| <code>quiesce-input</code> | <code>active|parked</code> → <code>quiescing</code>; <code>input_closed</code> | <code>control</code>; UTF-8 <code>terminal_instance_id + \"/quiesce/\" + quiescence_generation</code> | receipt precedes input closure; identical retry replays; uncertainty uses <code>status</code>; evidence binds closure time/generation | <code>input_quiescence</code> | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1188|| <code>wait-safe-boundary</code> | <code>quiescing</code> → <code>quiescing</code>; <code>safe_boundary_observed</code> | <code>control</code>; UTF-8 <code>terminal_instance_id + \"/boundary/\" + quiescence_generation + \"/\" + provider_proof_kind</code> | lesser of request deadline and timeout; identical retry returns the same proof; no proof on timeout; safe-boundary evidence | <code>safe_boundary_observation</code>; also <code>provider_process_observation</code> for provider proof kinds | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>quiesce_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1189|| <code>request-stop</code> | <code>quiescing</code> → <code>stopped</code>; <code>graceful_stop_requested,process_closed,backend_store_closed</code> | <code>control</code>; UTF-8 <code>terminal_instance_id + \"/stop/\" + safe_boundary_evidence_id</code> | lesser deadline/timeout; lost result requires <code>status</code>, then same-key retry only if not closed; boundary and closure evidence | <code>graceful_stop</code> | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>stop_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1190|| <code>terminate-stale</code> | <code>stale_fenced|unavailable</code> → <code>stopped</code>; <code>stale_incarnation_terminated,process_closed</code> | <code>force_stale</code>; UTF-8 <code>terminal_instance_id + \"/terminate/\" + stale_lease_id + \"/\" + decimal(stale_epoch)</code> | deadline may leave uncertain closure; use <code>status</code> before same-key retry; diagnostic, fencing, and closure evidence | <code>stale_process_termination</code> and <code>provider_process_observation</code> | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1191|| <code>restore</code> | <code>absent|stopped|unavailable</code> → <code>parked</code>; <code>binding_persisted,wrapper_restored</code> | <code>restore</code>; UTF-8 <code>session_id + \"/\" + bootstrap_operation_id</code> | persist receipt before restore; identical retry replays; uncertainty uses <code>status</code>; prior binding, Checkpoint, new binding, capability/credential evidence | <code>reboot_restoration</code>; <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> when credentials are required | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_restore_mismatch</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unavailable</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1192|\n1193|Create is idempotent on <code>(session_id, bootstrap_operation_id)</code> across\n1194|controller crash and lost result. AX and backend durably bind the pair before\n1195|the first child side effect. Identical retry returns the one result/instance;\n1196|a changed operation in the bootstrap window is <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>.\n1197|Only a successful status read proves absence. Attach is ownership-observational\n1198|for current-owner resume, local/remote/web, reconnect, and multi-attach.\n1199|\n1200|### 4.D Closed capabilities and evidence\n1201|\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
