the exact\n1409|tmux server generation, provider build, and macOS version. Aqua alone and\n1410|sentinel-only evidence are insufficient. Any provider flow requiring GUI\n1411|interaction, Keychain UI, a permission prompt, or other human action fails\n1412|closed until that interaction succeeds in the verified GUI realm.\n1413|\n1414|After restore, the wrapper MUST:\n1415|\n1416|1. read the latest locally known lease;\n1417|2. attempt a mesh lease refresh without blocking forever;\n1418|3. resume locally only if the local host has the winning lease and the required\n1419|   materialization is valid;\n1420|4. offer remote attach/takeover when another host owns the session in an\n1421|   interactive terminal; or\n1422|5. enter <code>parked</code> without launching the provider in all other cases.\n1423|\n1424|Logout or reboot invalidates unrenewed realm evidence. Without a verified GUI\n1425|realm, recovery MUST remain parked until GUI login re-establishes the broker,\n1426|functional sentinel, provider-auth smoke, and their generation/build/version\n1427|binding. A cached sentinel or prior <code>managername</code> observation MUST\n1428|NOT authorize resume.\n1429|\n1430|### 4.3 Native Windows backend\n1431|\n1432|Native Windows PowerShell MUST use a Windows terminal backend implemented with\n1433|Go process supervision and ConPTY. It MUST support mesh sync, workspace and\n1434|provider materialization, direct/provider resume, task-board open/adopt, remote\n1435|attach, graceful takeover when the provider row passes ConPTY gates, force\n1436|takeover, stop, and continuation.\n1437|\n1438|Native Windows MUST NOT claim tmux or tmux resurrection. A reboot destroys the\n1439|live ConPTY. The user service MUST recreate <code>ax pane SESSION_ID</code>,\n1440|which resumes from the latest valid checkpoint only after lease validation.\n1441|Terminal scrollback and live process memory are not portable state.\n1442|\n1443|Full tmux restore on a Windows computer is a WSL2 feature and uses the Linux\n1444|paths, process model, and provider installation inside that distribution. A\n1445|native Windows provider store and a WSL2 provider store are distinct\n1446|materialization targets.\n1447|\n1448|### 4.4 User services\n1449|\n1450|The background service integration is:\n1451|\n1452|- a launchd agent on macOS;\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
