{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cc7d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b0ab-f92f-74d3-a245-61ad42401b4b"},"sequence":1177,"recorded_at":1780531400002349,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"8ab0c8df-167f-48db-b83c-f756aeede0a9","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"8ab0c8df-167f-48db-b83c-f756aeede0a9","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"8ab0c8df-167f-48db-b83c-f756aeede0a9"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b0b0-c4fe-7352-a563-260024144a73"},"task_id":"01a0b0b0-c4fe-7352-a563-260024144a73","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b0b0-c4fe-7352-a563-260024144a73","chunk":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(1728 line(s) above)\n1729|### 5.2 Session Event\n1730|\n1731|This subsection defines the immutable Session Event <code>1.0.0</code> base\n1732|variant used for post-creation changes under Session Record 1. It uses schema\n1733|<code>urn:ax:schema:session-event</code> version <code>1.0.0</code>. Sections\n1734|13.14.5 and 13.15 define the independently closed <code>2.0.0</code> and\n1735|<code>3.0.0</code> event variants; a reader MUST select the exact registered\n1736|major and MUST NOT interpret this base definition as their complete schema.\n1737|\n1738|Required fields are <code>event_id</code> digest, <code>subject_id</code> and\n1739|<code>session_id</code> with the same UUID,\n1740|<code>event_type</code>, <code>created_by_host_id</code>,\n1741|<code>lease_epoch</code>, <code>lease_id</code>, and\n1742|<code>lease_sequence</code> as a uint53 starting at 1 for\n1743|each lease,\n1744|<code>predecessors</code> as a sorted array of one or more record/event digests,\n1745|<code>created_at</code>, and <code>payload</code>. The first event after\n1746|creation MUST have exactly the Session Record ID in\n1747|<code>predecessors</code>; later events reference one or more prior event heads.\n1748|Events form a DAG; they are not ordered by timestamp.\n1749|The exact top-level shape also requires <code>schema</code>,\n1750|<code>schema_version</code>, and <code>extensions</code>; no other top-level\n1751|member is permitted.\n1752|\n1753|The winning owner MUST serialize state-changing events for a session. Within\n1754|one lease, <code>lease_sequence</code> MUST increase by exactly one and each\n1755|event MUST reference the immediately prior authoritative event. The first event\n1756|under a successor lease uses sequence 1 and references the predecessor\n1757|checkpoint's authoritative event heads. A missing sequence, two different\n1758|events at one sequence under the winning lease, or an event that omits the\n1759|required predecessor is <code>invalid_state_transition</code>; the session MUST\n1760|park and MUST NOT accept input until a newer explicit takeover establishes an\n1761|unambiguous checkpoint. Losing-lease branches remain preserved but are never\n1762|applied to authoritative state.\n1763|\n1764|The v1 event types are:\n1765|\n1766|<code>session.created</code>, <code>terminal.created</code>,\n1767|<code>provider.launched</code>, <code>provider.identified</code>,\n1768|<code>session.idle</code>, <code>session.quiescing</code>,\n1769|<code>checkpoint.created</code>, <code>sync.completed</code>,\n1770|<code>session.stopped</code>, <code>session.resumed</code>,\n1771|<code>session.bootstrap_aborted</code>,\n1772|<code>lease.transferred</code>, <code>lease.forced</code>,\n1773|<code>session.parked</code>, <code>session.failed</code>,\n1774|<code>fork.created</code>, <code>profile.changed</code>,\n1775|<code>session.tombstoned</code>, <code>takeover.force_confirmed</code>,\n1776|<code>replica.replace_confirmed</code>, <code>task_board.launched</code>,\n1777|<code>task_board.adopted</code>, <code>tombstone.issued</code>, and\n1778|<code>tombstone.resolved</code>.\n1779|\n1780|The <code>payload</code> object is a closed tagged union selected by\n1781|<code>event_type</code>. It MUST contain exactly the members in this table; a\n1782|member shown as nullable remains required:\n1783|\n1784|| Event type | Exact payload members |\n1785|| --- | --- |\n1786|| <code>session.created</code> | <code>session_record_id:digest</code>, <code>bootstrap_operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>first_checkpoint_operation_id:UUIDv7</code> |\n1787|| <code>terminal.created</code> | <code>backend:tmux&#124;conpty</code>, <code>terminal_id:string[1..512]</code> |\n1788|| <code>provider.launched</code> | <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>, <code>provider_version:string[1..128]</code>, <code>execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo</code>, <code>profile_source_event_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>profile_mapping:string[1..512]</code> |\n1789|| <code>provider.identified</code> | <code>provider_identity_record_id:digest</code>, <code>confidence:exact&#124;strong&#124;weak</code> |\n1790|| <code>session.idle</code> | <code>boundary_ref:string[1..1024]</code>, <code>foreground_idle:boolean</code>, <code>background_idle:boolean</code> |\n1791|| <code>session.quiescing</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>reason:graceful_takeover&#124;stop&#124;checkpoint</code>, <code>input_blocked:boolean</code> |\n1792|| <code>checkpoint.created</code> | <code>checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>kind:periodic&#124;pre_stop&#124;closure&#124;fork_base&#124;manual</code> |\n1793|| <code>sync.completed</code> | <code>peer_host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>manifest_ids:sorted unique digest[1..1024]</code>, <code>materialized:boolean</code> |\n1794|| <code>session.stopped</code> | <code>graceful:boolean</code>, <code>checkpoint_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>resumable:boolean</code>, <code>closure_kind:checkpointed&#124;bootstrap_abort</code>, <code>process_closed:boolean</code>, <code>store_closed:boolean</code> |\n1795|| <code>session.resumed</code> | <code>checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo</code>, <code>profile_source_event_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>terminal_backend:tmux&#124;conpty</code>, <code>native_session_id:string[1..512]</code> |\n1796|| <code>session.bootstrap_aborted</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>failure_phase:before_terminal&#124;after_terminal&#124;after_process&#124;after_identity&#124;before_checkpoint</code>, <code>provider_identity_record_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>manager_session_ref:string[1..512]&#124;null</code>, <code>process_closed:boolean</code>, <code>store_closed:boolean</code>, <code>resume_allowed:false</code> |\n1797|| <code>lease.transferred</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>from_host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>to_host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>predecessor_lease_id:UUIDv4</code>, <code>new_lease_id:UUIDv4</code> |\n1798|| <code>lease.forced</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>expected_owner_host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>expected_epoch:uint53</code>, <code>new_lease_id:UUIDv4</code>, <code>checkpoint_id:digest</code> |\n1799|| <code>session.parked</code> | <code>reason:remote_owner&#124;stale_owner&#124;restore_policy&#124;failed_handoff</code>, <code>winning_lease_id:UUIDv4</code> |\n1800|| <code>session.failed</code> | <code>error_code:string[1..128]</code>, <code>retryable:boolean</code>, <code>operation_id:UUIDv7&#124;null</code> |\n1801|| <code>fork.created</code> | <code>source_session_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>source_checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>new_session_record_id:digest</code>, <code>provider_fork_mode:native&#124;supported_import&#124;task_board_clone</code>, <code>execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo</code>, <code>profile_source_event_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>source_profile_event_id:digest&#124;null</code> |\n1802|| <code>profile.changed</code> | <code>from:standard&#124;yolo</code>, <code>to:standard&#124;yolo</code>, <code>confirmed:boolean</code> |\n1803|| <code>session.tombstoned</code> | <code>tombstone_id:digest</code> |\n1804|| <code>takeover.force_confirmed</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>expected_owner_host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>expected_epoch:uint53</code>, <code>checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>accepted_risks:sorted unique enum[3]</code>, <code>confirmation_mode:interactive&#124;non_interactive</code> |\n1805|| <code>replica.replace_confirmed</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>workspace_group_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>target_host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>managed_replica_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>expected_marker_id:digest</code>, <code>expected_checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>replacement_checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>confirmation_mode:interactive&#124;non_interactive</code> |\n1806|| <code>task_board.launched</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>manager_session_ref:string[1..512]</code>, <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>, <code>launch_mode:primary_owner&#124;tracked_prompt</code>, <code>lease_epoch:uint53&gt;0</code>, <code>lease_id:UUIDv4</code>, <code>execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo</code>, <code>profile_source_event_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>board_goal_id:string[1..128]&#124;null</code>, <code>board_goal_revision:uint53&#124;null</code>, <code>state:running&#124;idle</code> |\n1807|| <code>task_board.adopted</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>bundle_id:digest</code>, <code>manager_session_ref:string[1..512]</code>, <code>board_goal_id:string[1..128]&#124;null</code>, <code>board_goal_revision:uint53&#124;null</code> |\n1808|| <code>tombstone.issued</code> | <code>tombstone_id:digest</code>, <code>scope:session&#124;workspace_entry&#124;provider_snapshot&#124;managed_replica</code>, <code>subject_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>target_ref:string[1..1024]</code> |\n1809|| <code>tombstone.resolved</code> | <code>tombstone_id:digest</code>, <code>resolution:deleted&#124;already_absent&#124;resurrected&#124;retained_conflict</code>, <code>target_ref:string[1..1024]</code>, <code>resulting_entry_digest:digest&#124;null</code> |\n1810|\n1811|For <code>takeover.force_confirmed</code>, <code>accepted_risks</code> MUST be\n1812|exactly <code>[\"divergent_history\",\"split_brain\",\"stale_process\"]</code> in\n1813|bytewise order. For <code>task_board.launched</code> and\n1814|<code>task_board.adopted</code>, goal ID and revision MUST\n1815|either both be null or both be non-null, and a non-null revision is greater\n1816|than zero. A <code>task_board.launched</code> event MUST repeat the winning\n1817|creation lease and the Session Record's provider/launch mode; a mismatch is\n1818|<code>integrity_failure</code>. Audit event issuance and retention are specified\n1819|in Sections 10.7 and 18.4. A <code>tombstone.resolved</code> resurrection\n1820|requires a non-null resulting entry digest; every other resolution requires\n1821|null.\n1822|\n1823|The profile and profile-source pair in every launch, resume, and fork event\n1824|MUST equal the Section 2.4 effective profile at the referenced checkpoint or,\n1825|for the first launch, the Session Record and null. A non-null source MUST name\n1826|the newest authoritative <code>profile.changed</code> event in that event-head\n1827|closure. Equal provider mapping strings do not permit changing either value.\n1828|For <code>fork.created</code>, the effective new-session authority is its newly\n1829|persisted Session Record, so <code>profile_source_event_id</code> is null.\n1830|<code>source_profile_event_id</code> separately equals the nullable source-\n1831|checkpoint profile event and never participates in new-session derivation.\n1832|\n1833|A <code>session.stopped</code> payload is <code>checkpointed</code> exactly when\n1834|<code>checkpoint_id</code> is non-null and <code>resumable = true</code>.\n1835|<code>bootstrap_abort</code> requires a null checkpoint, false resumable and\n1836|graceful values, and a preceding or equal-operation\n1837|<code>session.bootstrap_aborted</code> event; its derived lifecycle is\n1838|<code>failed</code>, never <code>stopped</code>. A bootstrap-aborted event\n1839|requires both closure booleans true. Its identity fields are both null before\n1840|identity, and after identity exactly the field belonging to the Session Record\n1841|kind is non-null. An ambiguous live process or open store cannot be represented\n1842|as a successful abort and remains <code>failed</code> with recovery diagnostics.\n1843|\n1844|An unknown event type MUST be retained as an immutable object but MUST NOT\n1845|change derived session state under major version 1.\n1846|\n1847|Normative example:\n1848|\n1849|~~~json\n1850|{\n1851|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:session-event\",\n1852|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n1853|  \"event_id\": \"sha256:46d2745fe7dfce856027be36e34f1cc6a56ffc846063dc4aa6aabf3f5a85bacb\",\n1854|  \"subject_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n1855|  \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n1856|  \"event_type\": \"session.stopped\",\n1857|  \"created_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-4a10-7b22-8b3c-1234567890ab\",\n1858|  \"lease_epoch\": 4,\n1859|  \"lease_id\": \"aaaaaaaa-bbbb-4ccc-8ddd-eeeeeeeeeeee\",\n1860|  \"lease_sequence\": 12,\n1861|  \"predecessors\": [\n1862|    \"sha256:7777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777\"\n1863|  ],\n1864|  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:08:00.000Z\",\n1865|  \"payload\": {\n1866|    \"graceful\": true,\n1867|    \"checkpoint_id\": \"sha256:e051996f51f13ace4f5cdebe1e30fd26fd5fe104cfd6e6a7f9f1206ba3819656\",\n1868|    \"resumable\": true,\n1869|    \"closure_kind\": \"checkpointed\",\n1870|    \"process_closed\": true,\n1871|    \"store_closed\": true\n1872|  },\n1873|  \"extensions\": {}\n1874|}\n1875|~~~\n1876|\n1877|#### Session Event 4.0.0 Terminal Instance events\n1878|\n1879|Session Event 4.0.0 retains the exact v3 top-level closed shape, digest rules,\n1880|lease ordering, predecessor rules, and complete v1-v3 event-type registry. It\n1881|changes exactly the payload definitions for <code>terminal.created</code> and\n1882|<code>session.resumed</code>; every other v1-v3 payload remains byte-for-byte\n1883|the definition selected by v3. The two v4 payloads are:\n1884|\n1885|| Event type | Exact payload members |\n1886|| --- | --- |\n1887|| <code>terminal.created</code> | <code>terminal_binding_id:digest</code>, <code>terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id</code>, <code>implementation_version:semver</code>, <code>protocol_version:semver</code>, <code>evidence_ids:sorted unique digest[1..256]</code> |\n1888|| <code>session.resumed</code> | <code>checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo</code>, <code>profile_source_event_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>terminal_binding_id:digest</code>, <code>terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id</code>, <code>implementation_version:semver</code>, <code>protocol_version:semver</code>, <code>evidence_ids:sorted unique digest[1..256]</code> |\n1889|\n1890|The binding digest is an opaque audit reference to a host-local Terminal\n1891|Instance Binding; the binding object itself is not an event member and is not\n1892|replicated. The evidence IDs MUST resolve locally to validated, sanitized\n1893|Manifest, Probe, and applicable Capability Evidence objects bound to the event's\n1894|backend ID and versions. They MUST NOT resolve through the event to a native\n1895|reference, generation string, socket, pipe, endpoint, token, credential,\n1896|terminal output, PID/handle, or live-process fact.\n1897|\n1898|<code>terminal.created</code> records the backend selected for a new AX-\n1899|authorized activation. <code>session.resumed</code> records the backend used by\n1900|that owner resume. A valid takeover or owner resume MAY select a different\n1901|admitted destination backend and emits a new binding digest and v4 event; it\n1902|does not clone/fork the LogicalSession and never mutates an earlier event.\n1903|Attach or presentation-client activity emits neither event and cannot change\n1904|Owner/Replica, lease, or fencing state. A reader of v1-v3 may retain a v4 event\n1905|as inert immutable history but MUST NOT derive runtime state or write a lower-\n1906|version replacement.\n1907|\n1908|### 5.3 Lease Record and ownership\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cc7f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b0ab-f92f-74d3-a245-61ad42401b4b"},"sequence":1178,"recorded_at":1780531400002351,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"8ab0c8df-167f-48db-b83c-f756aeede0a9","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"8ab0c8df-167f-48db-b83c-f756aeede0a9","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"8ab0c8df-167f-48db-b83c-f756aeede0a9"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b0b0-c4fe-7352-a563-260024144a73"},"task_id":"01a0b0b0-c4fe-7352-a563-260024144a73","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"01a0b0b0-c4fe-7352-a563-260024144a73"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cc81","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b0ab-f92f-74d3-a245-61ad42401b4b"},"sequence":1179,"recorded_at":1780531400002353,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"8ab0c8df-167f-48db-b83c-f756aeede0a9","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"8ab0c8df-167f-48db-b83c-f756aeede0a9","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"8ab0c8df-167f-48db-b83c-f756aeede0a9"},"call_id":"call_01a0b0b0be6c73058bb95065172986ab","text":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(1728 line(s) above)\n1729|### 5.2 Session Event\n1730|\n1731|This subsection defines the immutable Session Event <code>1.0.0</code> base\n1732|variant used for post-creation changes under Session Record 1. It uses schema\n1733|<code>urn:ax:schema:session-event</code> version <code>1.0.0</code>. Sections\n1734|13.14.5 and 13.15 define the independently closed <code>2.0.0</code> and\n1735|<code>3.0.0</code> event variants; a reader MUST select the exact registered\n1736|major and MUST NOT interpret this base definition as their complete schema.\n1737|\n1738|Required fields are <code>event_id</code> digest, <code>subject_id</code> and\n1739|<code>session_id</code> with the same UUID,\n1740|<code>event_type</code>, <code>created_by_host_id</code>,\n1741|<code>lease_epoch</code>, <code>lease_id</code>, and\n1742|<code>lease_sequence</code> as a uint53 starting at 1 for\n1743|each lease,\n1744|<code>predecessors</code> as a sorted array of one or more record/event digests,\n1745|<code>created_at</code>, and <code>payload</code>. The first event after\n1746|creation MUST have exactly the Session Record ID in\n1747|<code>predecessors</code>; later events reference one or more prior event heads.\n1748|Events form a DAG; they are not ordered by timestamp.\n1749|The exact top-level shape also requires <code>schema</code>,\n1750|<code>schema_version</code>, and <code>extensions</code>; no other top-level\n1751|member is permitted.\n1752|\n1753|The winning owner MUST serialize state-changing events for a session. Within\n1754|one lease, <code>lease_sequence</code> MUST increase by exactly one and each\n1755|event MUST reference the immediately prior authoritative event. The first event\n1756|under a successor lease uses sequence 1 and references the predecessor\n1757|checkpoint's authoritative event heads. A missing sequence, two different\n1758|events at one sequence under the winning lease, or an event that omits the\n1759|required predecessor is <code>invalid_state_transition</code>; the session MUST\n1760|park and MUST NOT accept input until a newer explicit takeover establishes an\n1761|unambiguous checkpoint. Losing-lease branches remain preserved but are never\n1762|applied to authoritative state.\n1763|\n1764|The v1 event types are:\n1765|\n1766|<code>session.created</code>, <code>terminal.created</code>,\n1767|<code>provider.launched</code>, <code>provider.identified</code>,\n1768|<code>session.idle</code>, <code>session.quiescing</code>,\n1769|<code>checkpoint.created</code>, <code>sync.completed</code>,\n1770|<code>session.stopped</code>, <code>session.resumed</code>,\n1771|<code>session.bootstrap_aborted</code>,\n1772|<code>lease.transferred</code>, <code>lease.forced</code>,\n1773|<code>session.parked</code>, <code>session.failed</code>,\n1774|<code>fork.created</code>, <code>profile.changed</code>,\n1775|<code>session.tombstoned</code>, <code>takeover.force_confirmed</code>,\n1776|<code>replica.replace_confirmed</code>, <code>task_board.launched</code>,\n1777|<code>task_board.adopted</code>, <code>tombstone.issued</code>, and\n1778|<code>tombstone.resolved</code>.\n1779|\n1780|The <code>payload</code> object is a closed tagged union selected by\n1781|<code>event_type</code>. It MUST contain exactly the members in this table; a\n1782|member shown as nullable remains required:\n1783|\n1784|| Event type | Exact payload members |\n1785|| --- | --- |\n1786|| <code>session.created</code> | <code>session_record_id:digest</code>, <code>bootstrap_operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>first_checkpoint_operation_id:UUIDv7</code> |\n1787|| <code>terminal.created</code> | <code>backend:tmux&#124;conpty</code>, <code>terminal_id:string[1..512]</code> |\n1788|| <code>provider.launched</code> | <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>, <code>provider_version:string[1..128]</code>, <code>execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo</code>, <code>profile_source_event_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>profile_mapping:string[1..512]</code> |\n1789|| <code>provider.identified</code> | <code>provider_identity_record_id:digest</code>, <code>confidence:exact&#124;strong&#124;weak</code> |\n1790|| <code>session.idle</code> | <code>boundary_ref:string[1..1024]</code>, <code>foreground_idle:boolean</code>, <code>background_idle:boolean</code> |\n1791|| <code>session.quiescing</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>reason:graceful_takeover&#124;stop&#124;checkpoint</code>, <code>input_blocked:boolean</code> |\n1792|| <code>checkpoint.created</code> | <code>checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>kind:periodic&#124;pre_stop&#124;closure&#124;fork_base&#124;manual</code> |\n1793|| <code>sync.completed</code> | <code>peer_host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>manifest_ids:sorted unique digest[1..1024]</code>, <code>materialized:boolean</code> |\n1794|| <code>session.stopped</code> | <code>graceful:boolean</code>, <code>checkpoint_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>resumable:boolean</code>, <code>closure_kind:checkpointed&#124;bootstrap_abort</code>, <code>process_closed:boolean</code>, <code>store_closed:boolean</code> |\n1795|| <code>session.resumed</code> | <code>checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo</code>, <code>profile_source_event_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>terminal_backend:tmux&#124;conpty</code>, <code>native_session_id:string[1..512]</code> |\n1796|| <code>session.bootstrap_aborted</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>failure_phase:before_terminal&#124;after_terminal&#124;after_process&#124;after_identity&#124;before_checkpoint</code>, <code>provider_identity_record_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>manager_session_ref:string[1..512]&#124;null</code>, <code>process_closed:boolean</code>, <code>store_closed:boolean</code>, <code>resume_allowed:false</code> |\n1797|| <code>lease.transferred</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>from_host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>to_host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>predecessor_lease_id:UUIDv4</code>, <code>new_lease_id:UUIDv4</code> |\n1798|| <code>lease.forced</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>expected_owner_host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>expected_epoch:uint53</code>, <code>new_lease_id:UUIDv4</code>, <code>checkpoint_id:digest</code> |\n1799|| <code>session.parked</code> | <code>reason:remote_owner&#124;stale_owner&#124;restore_policy&#124;failed_handoff</code>, <code>winning_lease_id:UUIDv4</code> |\n1800|| <code>session.failed</code> | <code>error_code:string[1..128]</code>, <code>retryable:boolean</code>, <code>operation_id:UUIDv7&#124;null</code> |\n1801|| <code>fork.created</code> | <code>source_session_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>source_checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>new_session_record_id:digest</code>, <code>provider_fork_mode:native&#124;supported_import&#124;task_board_clone</code>, <code>execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo</code>, <code>profile_source_event_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>source_profile_event_id:digest&#124;null</code> |\n1802|| <code>profile.changed</code> | <code>from:standard&#124;yolo</code>, <code>to:standard&#124;yolo</code>, <code>confirmed:boolean</code> |\n1803|| <code>session.tombstoned</code> | <code>tombstone_id:digest</code> |\n1804|| <code>takeover.force_confirmed</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>expected_owner_host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>expected_epoch:uint53</code>, <code>checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>accepted_risks:sorted unique enum[3]</code>, <code>confirmation_mode:interactive&#124;non_interactive</code> |\n1805|| <code>replica.replace_confirmed</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>workspace_group_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>target_host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>managed_replica_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>expected_marker_id:digest</code>, <code>expected_checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>replacement_checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>confirmation_mode:interactive&#124;non_interactive</code> |\n1806|| <code>task_board.launched</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>manager_session_ref:string[1..512]</code>, <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>, <code>launch_mode:primary_owner&#124;tracked_prompt</code>, <code>lease_epoch:uint53&gt;0</code>, <code>lease_id:UUIDv4</code>, <code>execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo</code>, <code>profile_source_event_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>board_goal_id:string[1..128]&#124;null</code>, <code>board_goal_revision:uint53&#124;null</code>, <code>state:running&#124;idle</code> |\n1807|| <code>task_board.adopted</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>bundle_id:digest</code>, <code>manager_session_ref:string[1..512]</code>, <code>board_goal_id:string[1..128]&#124;null</code>, <code>board_goal_revision:uint53&#124;null</code> |\n1808|| <code>tombstone.issued</code> | <code>tombstone_id:digest</code>, <code>scope:session&#124;workspace_entry&#124;provider_snapshot&#124;managed_replica</code>, <code>subject_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>target_ref:string[1..1024]</code> |\n1809|| <code>tombstone.resolved</code> | <code>tombstone_id:digest</code>, <code>resolution:deleted&#124;already_absent&#124;resurrected&#124;retained_conflict</code>, <code>target_ref:string[1..1024]</code>, <code>resulting_entry_digest:digest&#124;null</code> |\n1810|\n1811|For <code>takeover.force_confirmed</code>, <code>accepted_risks</code> MUST be\n1812|exactly <code>[\"divergent_history\",\"split_brain\",\"stale_process\"]</code> in\n1813|bytewise order. For <code>task_board.launched</code> and\n1814|<code>task_board.adopted</code>, goal ID and revision MUST\n1815|either both be null or both be non-null, and a non-null revision is greater\n1816|than zero. A <code>task_board.launched</code> event MUST repeat the winning\n1817|creation lease and the Session Record's provider/launch mode; a mismatch is\n1818|<code>integrity_failure</code>. Audit event issuance and retention are specified\n1819|in Sections 10.7 and 18.4. A <code>tombstone.resolved</code> resurrection\n1820|requires a non-null resulting entry digest; every other resolution requires\n1821|null.\n1822|\n1823|The profile and profile-source pair in every launch, resume, and fork event\n1824|MUST equal the Section 2.4 effective profile at the referenced checkpoint or,\n1825|for the first launch, the Session Record and null. A non-null source MUST name\n1826|the newest authoritative <code>profile.changed</code> event in that event-head\n1827|closure. Equal provider mapping strings do not permit changing either value.\n1828|For <code>fork.created</code>, the effective new-session authority is its newly\n1829|persisted Session Record, so <code>profile_source_event_id</code> is null.\n1830|<code>source_profile_event_id</code> separately equals the nullable source-\n1831|checkpoint profile event and never participates in new-session derivation.\n1832|\n1833|A <code>session.stopped</code> payload is <code>checkpointed</code> exactly when\n1834|<code>checkpoint_id</code> is non-null and <code>resumable = true</code>.\n1835|<code>bootstrap_abort</code> requires a null checkpoint, false resumable and\n1836|graceful values, and a preceding or equal-operation\n1837|<code>session.bootstrap_aborted</code> event; its derived lifecycle is\n1838|<code>failed</code>, never <code>stopped</code>. A bootstrap-aborted event\n1839|requires both closure booleans true. Its identity fields are both null before\n1840|identity, and after identity exactly the field belonging to the Session Record\n1841|kind is non-null. An ambiguous live process or open store cannot be represented\n1842|as a successful abort and remains <code>failed</code> with recovery diagnostics.\n1843|\n1844|An unknown event type MUST be retained as an immutable object but MUST NOT\n1845|change derived session state under major version 1.\n1846|\n1847|Normative example:\n1848|\n1849|~~~json\n1850|{\n1851|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:session-event\",\n1852|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n1853|  \"event_id\": \"sha256:46d2745fe7dfce856027be36e34f1cc6a56ffc846063dc4aa6aabf3f5a85bacb\",\n1854|  \"subject_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n1855|  \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n1856|  \"event_type\": \"session.stopped\",\n1857|  \"created_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-4a10-7b22-8b3c-1234567890ab\",\n1858|  \"lease_epoch\": 4,\n1859|  \"lease_id\": \"aaaaaaaa-bbbb-4ccc-8ddd-eeeeeeeeeeee\",\n1860|  \"lease_sequence\": 12,\n1861|  \"predecessors\": [\n1862|    \"sha256:7777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777\"\n1863|  ],\n1864|  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:08:00.000Z\",\n1865|  \"payload\": {\n1866|    \"graceful\": true,\n1867|    \"checkpoint_id\": \"sha256:e051996f51f13ace4f5cdebe1e30fd26fd5fe104cfd6e6a7f9f1206ba3819656\",\n1868|    \"resumable\": true,\n1869|    \"closure_kind\": \"checkpointed\",\n1870|    \"process_closed\": true,\n1871|    \"store_closed\": true\n1872|  },\n1873|  \"extensions\": {}\n1874|}\n1875|~~~\n1876|\n1877|#### Session Event 4.0.0 Terminal Instance events\n1878|\n1879|Session Event 4.0.0 retains the exact v3 top-level closed shape, digest rules,\n1880|lease ordering, predecessor rules, and complete v1-v3 event-type registry. It\n1881|changes exactly the payload definitions for <code>terminal.created</code> and\n1882|<code>session.resumed</code>; every other v1-v3 payload remains byte-for-byte\n1883|the definition selected by v3. The two v4 payloads are:\n1884|\n1885|| Event type | Exact payload members |\n1886|| --- | --- |\n1887|| <code>terminal.created</code> | <code>terminal_binding_id:digest</code>, <code>terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id</code>, <code>implementation_version:semver</code>, <code>protocol_version:semver</code>, <code>evidence_ids:sorted unique digest[1..256]</code> |\n1888|| <code>session.resumed</code> | <code>checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo</code>, <code>profile_source_event_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>terminal_binding_id:digest</code>, <code>terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id</code>, <code>implementation_version:semver</code>, <code>protocol_version:semver</code>, <code>evidence_ids:sorted unique digest[1..256]</code> |\n1889|\n1890|The binding digest is an opaque audit reference to a host-local Terminal\n1891|Instance Binding; the binding object itself is not an event member and is not\n1892|replicated. The evidence IDs MUST resolve locally to validated, sanitized\n1893|Manifest, Probe, and applicable Capability Evidence objects bound to the event's\n1894|backend ID and versions. They MUST NOT resolve through the event to a native\n1895|reference, generation string, socket, pipe, endpoint, token, credential,\n1896|terminal output, PID/handle, or live-process fact.\n1897|\n1898|<code>terminal.created</code> records the backend selected for a new AX-\n1899|authorized activation. <code>session.resumed</code> records the backend used by\n1900|that owner resume. A valid takeover or owner resume MAY select a different\n1901|admitted destination backend and emits a new binding digest and v4 event; it\n1902|does not clone/fork the LogicalSession and never mutates an earlier event.\n1903|Attach or presentation-client activity emits neither event and cannot change\n1904|Owner/Replica, lease, or fencing state. A reader of v1-v3 may retain a v4 event\n1905|as inert immutable history but MUST NOT derive runtime state or write a lower-\n1906|version replacement.\n1907|\n1908|### 5.3 Lease Record and ownership\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
