{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000ccaf","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b0ab-f92f-74d3-a245-61ad42401b4b"},"sequence":1202,"recorded_at":1780531400002399,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"8ab0c8df-167f-48db-b83c-f756aeede0a9","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"8ab0c8df-167f-48db-b83c-f756aeede0a9","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"8ab0c8df-167f-48db-b83c-f756aeede0a9"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b0b0-d371-7880-b39c-3ac9db6cd673"},"task_id":"01a0b0b0-d371-7880-b39c-3ac9db6cd673","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b0b0-d371-7880-b39c-3ac9db6cd673","chunk":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(2283 line(s) above)\n2284|### 5.7 Derived session states\n2285|\n2286|The state engine derives exactly one state for each\n2287|<code>(session_id, host_id)</code> projection and separately reports the\n2288|winning owner's projection as the session lifecycle state. Thus a destination\n2289|can be <code>running</code> while an old host is locally <code>stale</code>:\n2290|\n2291|| State | Meaning |\n2292|| --- | --- |\n2293|| <code>creating</code> | Session record and initial lease exist; no first validated checkpoint exists and bootstrap launch/retry is in progress |\n2294|| <code>running</code> | Winning owner has a live provider turn or accepts input |\n2295|| <code>idle</code> | Owner is live at an adapter-proven safe turn boundary |\n2296|| <code>quiescing</code> | New input is blocked while waiting for a safe boundary and clean stop |\n2297|| <code>checkpointing</code> | Safe state is being captured and validated |\n2298|| <code>stopped</code> | Winning owner has no provider process and a non-null validated checkpoint from which it is resumable |\n2299|| <code>materializing</code> | Destination staging/validation is in progress; it is not owner-active |\n2300|| <code>parked</code> | Wrapper exists but refuses provider launch due to remote/unknown ownership |\n2301|| <code>failed</code> | An operation failed and recovery metadata exists |\n2302|| <code>stale</code> | Local process/replica has a losing fencing token |\n2303|| <code>tombstoned</code> | Session is logically deleted and cannot resume |\n2304|\n2305|The exact <code>SessionState</code> enum is, in this order,\n2306|<code>creating</code>, <code>running</code>, <code>idle</code>,\n2307|<code>quiescing</code>, <code>checkpointing</code>, <code>stopped</code>,\n2308|<code>materializing</code>, <code>parked</code>, <code>failed</code>,\n2309|<code>stale</code>, and <code>tombstoned</code>. Every RPC and CLI field typed\n2310|<code>SessionState</code> uses exactly this registry. The spellings\n2311|<code>created</code>, <code>starting</code>, and <code>quiesced</code> are not\n2312|session lifecycle states in Session Record 1.0.0; a subsystem-specific bridge state\n2313|MAY use <code>quiesced</code> only where Section 9 declares that separate enum.\n2314|\n2315|Allowed transitions are:\n2316|\n2317|~~~text\n2318|creating -> running | idle | failed\n2319|running -> idle | quiescing | failed | stale\n2320|idle -> running | quiescing | checkpointing | stopped | stale\n2321|quiescing -> idle | checkpointing | failed | stale\n2322|checkpointing -> idle | stopped | materializing | failed\n2323|materializing -> stopped | running | parked | failed\n2324|stopped -> materializing | running | parked | tombstoned\n2325|parked -> materializing | running | stopped | stale\n2326|failed -> creating | stopped | parked | materializing | stale | tombstoned\n2327|stale -> stopped | tombstoned\n2328|~~~\n2329|\n2330|Any transition not listed MUST fail with <code>invalid_state_transition</code>.\n2331|Force takeover changes the old host's derived state to <code>stale</code> after\n2332|lease convergence even if its process remains alive.\n2333|\n2334|The <code>failed -> creating</code> edge is permitted only for an epoch-1\n2335|session with no validated checkpoint, the same winning create lease, no\n2336|authoritative <code>session.bootstrap_aborted</code> event, and the Section 13.1\n2337|bootstrap-retry preconditions. A force-closed bootstrap remains\n2338|<code>failed</code> and non-resumable. No event or RPC result may derive\n2339|<code>stopped</code> while <code>newest_checkpoint_id</code> is null.\n2340|\n2341|## 6. Configuration contract\n2342|\n2343|### 6.1 Loading and precedence\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
