cal process/replica has a losing fencing token |\n2303|| <code>tombstoned</code> | Session is logically deleted and cannot resume |\n2304|\n2305|The exact <code>SessionState</code> enum is, in this order,\n2306|<code>creating</code>, <code>running</code>, <code>idle</code>,\n2307|<code>quiescing</code>, <code>checkpointing</code>, <code>stopped</code>,\n2308|<code>materializing</code>, <code>parked</code>, <code>failed</code>,\n2309|<code>stale</code>, and <code>tombstoned</code>. Every RPC and CLI field typed\n2310|<code>SessionState</code> uses exactly this registry. The spellings\n2311|<code>created</code>, <code>starting</code>, and <code>quiesced</code> are not\n2312|session lifecycle states in Session Record 1.0.0; a subsystem-specific bridge state\n2313|MAY use <code>quiesced</code> only where Section 9 declares that separate enum.\n2314|\n2315|Allowed transitions are:\n2316|\n2317|~~~text\n2318|creating -> running | idle | failed\n2319|running -> idle | quiescing | failed | stale\n2320|idle -> running | quiescing | checkpointing | stopped | stale\n2321|quiescing -> idle | checkpointing | failed | stale\n2322|checkpointing -> idle | stopped | materializing | failed\n2323|materializing -> stopped | running | parked | failed\n2324|stopped -> materializing | running | parked | tombstoned\n2325|parked -> materializing | running | stopped | stale\n2326|failed -> creating | stopped | parked | materializing | stale | tombstoned\n2327|stale -> stopped | tombstoned\n2328|~~~\n2329|\n2330|Any transition not listed MUST fail with <code>invalid_state_transition</code>.\n2331|Force takeover changes the old host's derived state to <code>stale</code> after\n2332|lease convergence even if its process remains alive.\n2333|\n2334|The <code>failed -> creating</code> edge is permitted only for an epoch-1\n2335|session with no validated checkpoint, the same winning create lease, no\n2336|authoritative <code>session.bootstrap_aborted</code> event, and the Section 13.1\n2337|bootst