{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cce5","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b0ab-f92f-74d3-a245-61ad42401b4b"},"sequence":1229,"recorded_at":1780531400002453,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"8ab0c8df-167f-48db-b83c-f756aeede0a9","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"8ab0c8df-167f-48db-b83c-f756aeede0a9","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"8ab0c8df-167f-48db-b83c-f756aeede0a9"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b0b1-7eda-7d01-ae8b-b133509e22c6"},"task_id":"01a0b0b1-7eda-7d01-ae8b-b133509e22c6","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b0b1-7eda-7d01-ae8b-b133509e22c6","chunk":"Read text file `internal/sessprofile/profile.go`.\n(99 line(s) above)\n100|\tSchemaVersion   string\n101|\tSessionID       string\n102|\tCreatedByHostID string\n103|\tCreatedAt       string\n104|\tLeaseEpoch      uint64\n105|\tLeaseID         string\n106|\tSequence        uint64\n107|\tPredecessors    []string\n108|\tPayload         map[string]any\n109|}\n110|\n111|// LeaseHead is one observed fencing token: the winning-lease pair\n112|// carried by every owner-authored event and mutation.\n113|type LeaseHead struct {\n114|\tEpoch   uint64\n115|\tLeaseID string\n116|}\n117|\n118|// Derive folds one record with its authoritative events in chain\n119|// order into the session-head effective pair: the creation profile\n120|// while no authoritative profile.changed event exists, otherwise\n121|// the newest change's target with that event's digest as source.\n122|// An empty chain derives the creation pair. It is pure: no I/O, no\n123|// clock, no cache. Chain continuity is re-checked over the input,\n124|// so a chain-forbidden reordering refuses with\n125|// invalid_state_transition instead of silently deriving a different\n126|// pair, and a losing-lease or ambiguous event refuses instead of\n127|// changing the derivation.\n128|func Derive(record Record, events []Event) (Pair, error) {\n129|\tif err := checkRecord(record); err != nil {\n130|\t\treturn Pair{}, err\n131|\t}\n132|\tif len(events) == 0 {\n133|\t\treturn Pair{Profile: record.Creation}, nil\n134|\t}\n135|\tordered, err := checkChain(record, events, len(events))\n136|\tif err != nil {\n137|\t\treturn Pair{}, err\n138|\t}\n139|\treturn foldChanges(record.Creation, ordered, nil)\n140|}\n141|\n142|// DeriveForHeads derives the effective pair over the transitive\n143|// predecessor closure of heads: the Section 5.4 event-head closure\n144|// of one checkpoint. Only closure events are consulted — a later\n145|// local-only change outside the heads never affects the pair, and\n146|// the derivation never falls back to the creation value while the\n147|// closure holds a change. Events past the closure are not even\n148|// validated. An unknown head or a dangling predecessor contradicts\n149|// the admitted closure (integrity_failure); empty heads carry no\n150|// closure to derive over.\n151|func DeriveForHeads(record Record, events []Event, heads []string) (Pair, error) {\n152|\tif err := checkRecord(record); err != nil {\n153|\t\treturn Pair{}, err\n154|\t}\n155|\tif len(heads) == 0 {\n156|\t\treturn Pair{}, refuse(ErrDerivation, \"checkpoint closure names no event head\")\n157|\t}\n158|\tclosure, limit, err := closurePrefix(record.RecordID, events, heads)\n159|\tif err != nil {\n160|\t\treturn Pair{}, err\n161|\t}\n162|\tordered, err := checkChain(record, events, limit)\n163|\tif err != nil {\n164|\t\treturn Pair{}, err\n165|\t}\n166|\treturn foldChanges(record.Creation, ordered, closure)\n167|}\n168|\n169|// checkRecord validates the record surface the derivation reads:\n170|// session identity plus a creation profile inside the vocabulary.\n171|func checkRecord(record Record) error {\n172|\tif record.SessionID == \"\" || record.RecordID == \"\" {\n173|\t\treturn refuse(ErrInvalidRecord, \"reducer input carries no session identity\")\n174|\t}\n175|\tif record.Creation != ProfileStandard && record.Creation != ProfileYOLO {\n176|\t\treturn refuse(ErrInvalidRecord, \"session record carries creation profile %q, want standard|yolo\", record.Creation)\n177|\t}\n178|\treturn nil\n179|}\n180|\n181|// closurePrefix resolves the transitive predecessor closure of\n182|// heads against the chain index in input order. The Session Record\n183|// digest is the genesis terminal; every other predecessor must\n184|// name a chained event. It returns the closure set plus the\n185|// one-past-the-end validation limit: the highest closure position\n186|// plus one, so events past the closure are never consulted.\n187|func closurePrefix(recordID string, events []Event, heads []string) (map[string]bool, int, error) {\n188|\tbyID := make(map[string]Event, len(events))\n189|\tposition := make(map[string]int, len(events))\n190|\tfor index := range events {\n191|\t\tbyID[events[index].ID] = events[index]\n192|\t\tposition[events[index].ID] = index\n193|\t}\n194|\tfor _, head := range heads {\n195|\t\tif _, ok := byID[head]; !ok {\n196|\t\t\treturn nil, 0, refuse(ErrIntegrity, \"checkpoint closure names unknown event head %s\", head)\n197|\t\t}\n198|\t}\n199|\tclosure := make(map[string]bool, len(events))\n200|\tstack := append([]string(nil), heads...)\n201|\tfor len(stack) > 0 {\n202|\t\tid := stack[len(stack)-1]\n203|\t\tstack = stack[:len(stack)-1]\n204|\t\tif closure[id] {\n205|\t\t\tcontinue\n206|\t\t}\n207|\t\tevent, ok := byID[id]\n208|\t\tif !ok {\n209|\t\t\tif id == recordID {\n210|\t\t\t\tcontinue\n211|\t\t\t}\n212|\t\t\treturn nil, 0, refuse(ErrIntegrity, \"checkpoint closure names unknown event %s\", id)\n213|\t\t}\n214|\t\tclosure[id] = true\n215|\t\tstack = append(stack, event.Predecessors...)\n216|\t}\n217|\tlimit := 0\n218|\tfor id := range closure {\n219|\t\tif position[id]+1 > limit {\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
