{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cce9","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b0ab-f92f-74d3-a245-61ad42401b4b"},"sequence":1231,"recorded_at":1780531400002457,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"8ab0c8df-167f-48db-b83c-f756aeede0a9","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"8ab0c8df-167f-48db-b83c-f756aeede0a9","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"8ab0c8df-167f-48db-b83c-f756aeede0a9"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b0b1-7f75-74a2-94cc-8d3c01340f28"},"task_id":"01a0b0b1-7f75-74a2-94cc-8d3c01340f28","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b0b1-7f75-74a2-94cc-8d3c01340f28","chunk":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(625 line(s) above)\n626|### 2.4 Execution profiles\n627|\n628|The persisted profile enum is <code>standard</code> or <code>yolo</code>.\n629|<code>yolo</code> means the provider-specific unrestricted/no-approval mode; it\n630|does not mean that <code>ax</code> ignores its own ownership, conflict,\n631|allowlist, or integrity checks.\n632|\n633|The immutable Session Record stores the creation profile. Every\n634|<code>provider.launched</code>, <code>task_board.launched</code>,\n635|<code>session.resumed</code>, and <code>fork.created</code> event repeats the\n636|effective ax profile and the digest of the authoritative\n637|<code>profile.changed</code> event from which it was derived, or null when the\n638|Session Record is still the authority. A profile change requires\n639|<code>ax session set-profile NAME PROFILE</code>, a new event under the current\n640|lease, and operator confirmation when changing to <code>yolo</code>. A resume\n641|MUST fail with <code>profile_mapping_unavailable</code> if the adapter cannot\n642|map the stored profile for the probed provider version.\n643|\n644|The effective persisted profile is the Session Record value followed by the\n645|newest authoritative <code>profile.changed</code> event in lease/sequence order.\n646|Losing-lease or ambiguous events MUST NOT change it. Every command that says\n647|“persisted profile” refers to this derived value. The profile source is null\n648|when no authoritative change exists and otherwise is exactly that newest\n649|event's <code>event_id</code>. A Checkpoint's event-head closure fixes both\n650|values for that checkpoint; a bundle, resume, or fork MUST NOT fall back to the\n651|Session Record creation value when the closure contains a later change.\n652|\n653|Fork creates a new authority boundary. Its new Session Record stores the\n654|source-checkpoint effective profile as its creation profile, so the new\n655|session's <code>profile_source_event_id</code> is null. The\n656|<code>fork.created.source_profile_event_id</code> separately preserves the\n657|nullable source-session event used for that projection; it is provenance and\n658|MUST NOT be treated as a profile event in the new session's event chain.\n659|\n660|Provider mapping is evidence, not profile authority. In particular, Pi 0.73.1\n661|maps both ax profiles to <code>default_unrestricted_tool_set</code>; the two ax\n662|profiles remain distinct because the Session/Event authority and confirmation\n663|history remain distinct even when the provider mapping strings are equal.\n664|\n665|The following end-to-end profile fixtures are normative. Let P0 be the Session\n666|Record profile, E1 an authoritative <code>profile.changed</code> event to P1,\n667|and C1 a checkpoint whose event-head closure contains E1:\n668|\n669|| Fixture | Path | Required profile authority |\n670|| --- | --- | --- |\n671|| <code>PROFILE-DIRECT-TAKEOVER</code> | Direct start P0 → E1 → C1 → graceful/force takeover | Bundle is absent; materialization finalize, plugin resume, and resumed event all carry P1/E1 |\n672|| <code>PROFILE-DIRECT-RESUME</code> | Direct stop at C1 → owner resume | Plugin resume and resumed event carry P1/E1; creation P0 is ignored |\n673|| <code>PROFILE-DIRECT-FORK</code> | Fork C1 | New Session Record creation profile is P1; fork event carries P1/null as new-session authority plus <code>source_profile_event_id=E1</code>; resumed carries P1/null |\n674|| <code>PROFILE-TB-TAKEOVER</code> | Task-board start P0 → E1 → export C1 → takeover | Bundle projection carries P1/E1; journaled bridge resume and events use the same pair |\n675|| <code>PROFILE-TB-RESUME</code> | Task-board owner resume from C1 | Bundle, bridge resume, and events agree on P1/E1 |\n676|| <code>PROFILE-TB-FORK</code> | Task-board fork C1 | Source bundle carries P1/E1; new Session Record and bridge resume use P1/null; fork event retains E1 only in <code>source_profile_event_id</code> |\n677|| <code>PROFILE-PI-EQUAL-MAPPING</code> | Pi changes <code>standard</code> to <code>yolo</code> at E1 while both map to <code>default_unrestricted_tool_set</code> | Ax still persists and reports P1/E1; equal provider argv text is not authority to erase E1 |\n678|\n679|Any fixture that uses P0 after C1, omits E1 where the event schema requires its\n680|source, or accepts a bundle profile inconsistent with C1 is\n681|<code>integrity_failure</code> before activation.\n682|\n683|## 3. Architecture and durable local layout\n684|\n685|### 3.1 Required components\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
