lease epoch %d precedes chain head epoch %d\", event.ID, lease.Epoch, current.Epoch)\n289|\t\t}\n290|\t\tif !containsString(event.Predecessors, tailID) {\n291|\t\t\treturn nil, refuse(ErrInvalidTransition, \"event %s predecessors omit prior authoritative event\", event.ID)\n292|\t\t}\n293|\t\ttailID, tailSeq = event.ID, event.Sequence\n294|\t}\n295|\treturn ordered, nil\n296|}\n297|\n298|// foldChanges tracks the newest profile.changed event over the\n299|// validated prefix, restricted to the closure when non-nil. Every\n300|// other event type is inert. A change payload that no longer\n301|// decodes refuses integrity_failure: chained bytes passed the\n302|// closed shape at append time, so an undecodable member contradicts\n303|// the attested chain. Only the target feeds the derivation; the\n304|// confirmation history belongs to the publication flow that\n305|// admitted the event.\n306|func foldChanges(creation string, ordered []Event, closure map[string]bool) (Pair, error) {\n307|\tpair := Pair{Profile: creation}\n308|\tfor index := range ordered {\n309|\t\tevent := ordered[index]\n310|\t\tif closure != nil && !closure[event.ID] {\n311|\t\t\tcontinue\n312|\t\t}\n313|\t\tif event.Type != \"profile.changed\" {\n314|\t\t\tcontinue\n315|\t\t}\n316|\t\ttarget, err := changeTarget(event)\n317|\t\tif err != nil {\n318|\t\t\treturn Pair{}, err\n319|\t\t}\n320|\t\tpair = Pair{Profile: target, Source: event.ID, HasSource: true}\n321|\t}\n322|\treturn pair, nil\n323|}\n324|\n325|// changeTarget decodes the target profile of one validated\n326|// profile.changed event. The from/to/confirmed members mirror the\n327|// closed shape the canonical owner admitted: both ends inside the\n328|// vocabulary, from and to distinct, confirmed a boolean. The value\n329|// of confirmed never affects authority here.\n330|func changeTarget(event Event) (string, error) {\n331|\tfrom, ok := payloadString(event.Payload, \"from\")\n332|\tif !ok || (from != ProfileStandard && from != ProfileYOLO) {\n333|\t\treturn \"\", refuse(ErrIntegrity, \"event %s carries no valid change source for profile authority\", event.ID)\n334|\t}\n335|\ttarget, ok := payloadString(event.Payload, \"to\")\n336|\tif !ok || (target != ProfileStandard && target != ProfileYOLO) {\n337|\t\treturn \"\", refuse(ErrIntegrity, \"event %s carries no valid change target for profile authority\", event.ID)\n338|\t}\n339|\tif from == target {\n340|\t\treturn \"\", refuse(ErrIntegrity, \"event %s changes profile %q to itself for profile authority\", event.ID, from)\n341|\t}\n342|\tif _, ok := payloadBool(event.Payload, \"confirmed\"); !ok {\n343|\t\treturn \"\", refuse(ErrIntegrity, \"event %s carries no confirmation for profile authority\", event.ID)\n344|\t}\n345|\treturn target, nil\n346|}\n347|\n348|// payloadString reads one string member from an admitted payload.\n349|// The second result reports presence and type only; the caller\n350|// attributes the refusal.\n351|func payloadString(payload map[string]any, name string) (string, bool) {\n352|\tvalue, ok := payload[name]\n353|\tif !ok {\n354|\t\treturn \"\", false\n355|\t}\n356|\ttext, ok := value.(string)\n357|\treturn text, ok\n358|}\n359|\n360|// payloadBool reads one boolean member from an admitted payload.\n361|func payloadBool(payload map[string]any, name string) (bool, bool) {\n362|\tvalue, ok := payload[name]\n363|\tif !ok {\n364|\t\treturn false, false\n365|\t}\n366|\tflag, ok := value.(bool)\n367|\treturn flag, ok\n368|}\n369|\n370|// compareLease orders two lease heads by the Section 5.3 tuple\n371|// rule: the greatest (epoch, lease_id) wins, where lease_id uses\n372|// bytewise UUID order over canonical lowercase UUIDv4.\n373|func compareLease(a, b LeaseHead) int {\n374|\tif a.Epoch != b.Epoch {\n375|\t\tif a.Epoch < b.Epoch {\n376|\t\t\treturn -1\n377|\t\t}\n378|\t\treturn 1\n379|\t}\n380|\tswitch {\n381|\tcase a.LeaseID < b.LeaseID:\n382|\t\treturn -1\n383|\tcase a.LeaseID > b.LeaseID:\n384|\t\treturn 1\n385|\t}\n386|\treturn 0\n387|}\n388|\n389|func containsString(haystack []string, needle string) bool {\n390|\tfor _, candidate := range haystack {\n391|\t\tif candidate == needle {\n392|\t\t\treturn true\n393|\t\t}\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
