{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cd9b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b0ab-f92f-74d3-a245-61ad42401b4b"},"sequence":1320,"recorded_at":1780531400002635,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"8ab0c8df-167f-48db-b83c-f756aeede0a9","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"8ab0c8df-167f-48db-b83c-f756aeede0a9","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"8ab0c8df-167f-48db-b83c-f756aeede0a9"},"call_id":"call_01a0b0b3f2d276cf933244cd5b3b5e38","text":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(8992 line(s) above)\n8993|### 13.1 Direct-session launch\n8994|\n8995|Preconditions:\n8996|\n8997|- configuration and local host identity are valid;\n8998|- the session name is unused across the reachable mesh;\n8999|- the provider plugin is trusted and <code>probe</code> succeeds;\n9000|- requested profile mapping is available;\n9001|- destination workspace is validated or captured as a new managed workspace;\n9002|- the terminal backend is available; and\n9003|- no task-board fields are supplied.\n9004|\n9005|Transitions:\n9006|\n9007|1. Allocate session, caller-stable bootstrap-operation,\n9008|   first-checkpoint-operation, and initial lease IDs. If the workspace has a\n9009|   valid current managed-replica marker, reuse its unique Workspace Group\n9010|   Record after exact topology validation; otherwise allocate new workspace-\n9011|   group/workspace IDs and one new group record. Epoch is 1 and the local host\n9012|   is the holder.\n9013|2. Persist any new Workspace Group Record, then the Session Record referencing\n9014|   that group, the initial Lease Record, and <code>session.created</code> carrying\n9015|   both operation IDs before creating a process. Joining\n9016|   an existing group publishes no group update; derived membership changes by\n9017|   union of the new Session Record.\n9018|3. Create the durable terminal entry <code>ax pane SESSION_ID</code> with the\n9019|   bootstrap operation ID.\n9020|4. Call provider <code>launch</code> and validate its argv/env-name plan.\n9021|5. Start the provider through the terminal backend with the epoch-1 fencing\n9022|   token and persisted profile. Persist <code>provider.launched</code> with\n9023|   <code>execution_profile</code> equal to the Session Record and\n9024|   <code>profile_source_event_id = null</code>.\n9025|6. Call <code>identify-session</code>; persist the Provider Identity Record and\n9026|   <code>provider.identified</code> event.\n9027|7. When the first safe boundary is observed, create the workspace-group root\n9028|   manifest. If <code>portable_store</code> is enabled, call provider\n9029|   <code>native-store-plan phase=capture</code> and <code>capture</code> with the\n9030|   first-checkpoint operation ID into an\n9031|   isolated Object Sink; otherwise create a zero-entry provider manifest that\n9032|   references the exact Provider Identity Record. Validate both, then publish\n9033|   the direct-path checkpoint with a non-null provider manifest.\n9034|8. Publish immutable objects for replica sync and report <code>running</code>\n9035|   or <code>idle</code>.\n9036|\n9037|The first-checkpoint operation ID keys the capture/export and checkpoint-\n9038|publication transaction even when a backend-only provider emits a zero-entry\n9039|manifest. An identical retry reuses the same immutable objects and event;\n9040|changing either operation ID after <code>session.created</code> is\n9041|<code>idempotency_mismatch</code>.\n9042|\n9043|Until step 7 publishes the first Checkpoint, this is the closed\n9044|<em>bootstrap window</em>. The epoch-1 lease is authoritative with\n9045|<code>checkpoint_id = null</code>; the derived session state is\n9046|<code>creating</code> while a retry is eligible and <code>failed</code> after an\n9047|ambiguous/live-process error or explicit abort. No implementation may invent a\n9048|checkpoint ID or call that state <code>stopped</code>.\n9049|\n9050|Failure handling is phase-exact:\n9051|\n9052|| Fixture/boundary | Durable facts | Recovery |\n9053|| --- | --- | --- |\n9054|| <code>BOOT-DIRECT-BEFORE-TERMINAL</code> | Session/lease exist; no terminal, process, identity, or checkpoint | <code>ax resume</code> may retry terminal creation under the same IDs after probe; force stop emits bootstrap abort |\n9055|| <code>BOOT-DIRECT-AFTER-TERMINAL</code> | Wrapper exists; no provider process or checkpoint | Resume reuses that wrapper and retries launch once; force stop removes only the inert wrapper after closure proof |\n9056|| <code>BOOT-DIRECT-AFTER-PROCESS</code> | Provider may be live; no identified identity/checkpoint | Resume MUST first reconcile exact PID/PTY and bootstrap operation; if liveness/identity is ambiguous, remain failed and require stop/reconciliation rather than start a second process |\n9057|| <code>BOOT-DIRECT-AFTER-IDENTITY</code> | Identity/event exist; no checkpoint | Resume validates the same identity and continues capture; it MUST NOT call provider new-session launch |\n9058|| <code>BOOT-DIRECT-BEFORE-CHECKPOINT</code> | Captured objects may exist but no Checkpoint Record is authoritative | Validate/reuse immutable objects and publish the first checkpoint, or abort; objects are never relabeled as a checkpoint |\n9059|\n9060|A bootstrap retry is allowed only at epoch 1, with a null lease checkpoint,\n9061|no authoritative <code>session.bootstrap_aborted</code>, and either proven no\n9062|provider process or one exact reconciled process/identity from this launch.\n9063|The retry reuses every already persisted operation/terminal/provider identity\n9064|and is idempotent; it never creates a second raw provider process. A graceful\n9065|stop may first reach a safe boundary and publish the initial checkpoint, then\n9066|execute the ordinary checkpointed stop. A force stop may close the process and\n9067|emit <code>session.bootstrap_aborted</code> followed by\n9068|<code>session.stopped</code> with null checkpoint,\n9069|<code>resumable=false</code>, and <code>closure_kind=bootstrap_abort</code>; the\n9070|resulting lifecycle state is <code>failed</code>, not <code>stopped</code>.\n9071|Closure with an unknown/live process is unsuccessful and emits neither event.\n9072|\n9073|<code>BOOT-ABORT-CROSS-CONTRACT</code> is the exact successful force-closure\n9074|projection for a failure after process creation and before identity:\n9075|\n9076|| Surface | Exact authoritative values |\n9077|| --- | --- |\n9078|| <code>session.bootstrap_aborted</code> payload | <code>{operation_id:BOOTSTRAP_ID,failure_phase:after_process,provider_identity_record_id:null,manager_session_ref:null,process_closed:true,store_closed:true,resume_allowed:false}</code> |\n9079|| Following <code>session.stopped</code> payload | <code>{graceful:false,checkpoint_id:null,resumable:false,closure_kind:bootstrap_abort,process_closed:true,store_closed:true}</code> |\n9080|| RPC <code>session.stop</code> success | <code>{operation_id:STOP_ID,already_applied:false,closure:{process_closed:true,store_closed:true,exit_code:EXIT_OR_NULL,remaining_process_handles:[],final_store_generation:null},final_checkpoint_id:null,resumable:false,bootstrap_aborted:true,resulting_state:failed}</code> |\n9081|| CLI <code>stop</code> body | Exact failed <code>SessionSummary</code> with both newest-checkpoint members null, plus <code>{graceful:false,checkpoint_id:null,resumable:false,bootstrap_aborted:true,process_closed:true,store_closed:true}</code> |\n9082|\n9083|The event IDs and sequences are ordinary Section 5.2 identities. The RPC and\n9084|CLI operation ID is STOP_ID; the abort event retains BOOTSTRAP_ID so audit can\n9085|join the abandoned launch. <code>BOOT-ABORT-N1</code> changes any one null to a\n9086|digest, any closure boolean to false, resulting state to stopped, or resumable\n9087|to true; the attempted success MUST be rejected. After identity, exactly the\n9088|direct provider-identity or task-board manager-reference member becomes\n9089|non-null as Section 5.2 requires.\n9090|\n9091|The command MUST NOT delete the workspace, native provider bytes, or immutable\n9092|records during recovery. The initial lease remains authoritative until an\n9093|explicit later ownership operation.\n9094|\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
