{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cf49","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b0ab-f92f-74d3-a245-61ad42401b4b"},"sequence":1535,"recorded_at":1780531400003065,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"8ab0c8df-167f-48db-b83c-f756aeede0a9","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"8ab0c8df-167f-48db-b83c-f756aeede0a9","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"8ab0c8df-167f-48db-b83c-f756aeede0a9"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b0b9-f8b7-7dd3-879c-d2a0d3cf9148"},"task_id":"01a0b0b9-f8b7-7dd3-879c-d2a0d3cf9148","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b0b9-f8b7-7dd3-879c-d2a0d3cf9148","chunk":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(9851 line(s) above)\n9852|### 13.10 Resume\n9853|\n9854|<code>ax resume NAME</code> is allowed only on the winning owner host. A replica\n9855|receives <code>not_owner</code> and explicit attach/takeover/fork choices.\n9856|\n9857|The owner first refreshes lease knowledge and verifies its fencing token. If\n9858|the epoch-1 winning lease has a null checkpoint, resume is not an ordinary\n9859|resume: it executes only the Section 13.1/13.2 bootstrap retry predicate and\n9860|phase continuation. An authoritative bootstrap-abort event returns\n9861|<code>checkpoint_unavailable</code> and cannot be resumed. No later epoch may\n9862|have a null checkpoint.\n9863|\n9864|For a validated checkpoint, derive the exact effective profile/source from its\n9865|event-head closure, probe the mapping/capabilities, and choose exactly one path:\n9866|\n9867|1. <strong>No materialization.</strong> If the current managed marker and native\n9868|   provider/bridge status already equal the checkpoint and winning lease, do\n9869|   not create a transaction. Direct sessions validate native discovery, start\n9870|   <code>ax pane SESSION_ID</code>, invoke plugin resume with the effective\n9871|   profile, prove the process, and emit <code>session.resumed</code>. A\n9872|   task-board session validates the existing manager binding and calls the\n9873|   public bridge resume with a caller-stable ID/profile, proves status, and\n9874|   emits the event. A missing binding does not qualify for this path.\n9875|2. <strong>Direct materialization.</strong> Call tagged\n9876|   <code>materialize.prepare</code> with <code>intent=owner_resume</code>, the\n9877|   owner as the sole materialization member, empty ownership-transfer set, and\n9878|   workspace/provider/composite kind. Call commit and require durable\n9879|   <code>prepared</code>. Validate native discovery or exact backend identity,\n9880|   start the wrapper, invoke plugin resume, and prove the exact session. Then\n9881|   finalize with <code>direct_owner_resumed</code> and the effective\n9882|   profile/source; only a committed result permits <code>session.resumed</code>.\n9883|3. <strong>Task-board materialization.</strong> Prepare with task-board or\n9884|   composite kind and the same cohort rules. Commit installs the opaque bundle,\n9885|   imports, and opens dormant through the journal. Finalize with\n9886|   <code>task_board_owner_resumed</code>, the winning binding, and effective\n9887|   profile/source; finalize adopts/resumes and proves public bridge status.\n9888|   Only its committed result permits adoption/resume events.\n9889|\n9890|Every materializing path is therefore\n9891|prepare → commit/prepared → identity or dormant validation → activation →\n9892|finalize/committed. A response lost at any arrow is recovered with\n9893|<code>materialize.status</code> plus plugin/bridge status under the same IDs.\n9894|Before direct process start or task-board adopt, validation failure, operator\n9895|abort, or lease loss invokes rollback. After a direct process is proven running\n9896|or task-board adopt succeeds, ordinary byte rollback is forbidden: the same\n9897|owner must finish status/finalize, stop the activation, or perform a new fenced\n9898|ownership operation. Failure leaves the session stopped/failed on that same\n9899|owner and preserves the journal.\n9900|\n9901|Normative resume fixtures are:\n9902|\n9903|| Fixture | Kind/path | Required terminal result |\n9904|| --- | --- | --- |\n9905|| <code>RESUME-NO-MAT-DIRECT</code> | Current workspace/native identity; no transaction | Same lease/profile, exact provider resumed, one resumed event |\n9906|| <code>RESUME-WORKSPACE</code> | Workspace-only prepare/commit, direct native state already current | Marker committed after direct activation; provider transaction remains none |\n9907|| <code>RESUME-PROVIDER</code> | Provider-only prepared transaction | Null marker/path; provider transaction commits only after exact resume |\n9908|| <code>RESUME-COMPOSITE-DIRECT</code> | Workspace plus portable provider | Both roots prepared; exact provider running before finalize cleans backups |\n9909|| <code>RESUME-TASK-BOARD</code> | Task-board-only bundle | Journal opened → adopted → resumed; null marker/path |\n9910|| <code>RESUME-COMPOSITE-TB</code> | Workspace plus bundle | Workspace remains rollbackable until bridge resume proof; then marker/finalize |\n9911|| <code>RESUME-PRE-ACTIVATION-NEG</code> | Any prepared path fails validation | Roll back and remain stopped owner |\n9912|| <code>RESUME-POST-ACTIVATION-NEG</code> | Activation succeeds, response/finalize fails | Status-recover/finalize or explicitly stop; never roll back behind live activation |\n9913|\n9914|It MUST not create a new native session under the old logical identity.\n9915|Antigravity backend <code>not found</code> is\n9916|<code>unsupported_backend_identity</code>, not a successful blank resume.\n9917|\n9918|### 13.11 Reboot restore\n9919|\n9920|On wrapper/service restore:\n9921|\n9922|1. rebuild or validate the local derived index;\n9923|2. inspect every previously running/idle local session;\n9924|3. refresh lease heads when peers are reachable;\n9925|4. mark losing local processes stale;\n9926|5. for winning local owners, validate the newest checkpoint and persisted\n9927|   profile;\n9928|6. recreate tmux wrapper panes or native Windows ConPTY wrappers; and\n9929|7. auto-resume only sessions whose configuration explicitly enables\n9930|   <code>restore.auto_resume</code> and whose provider safe-stop/restore gate\n9931|   passed.\n9932|\n9933|Otherwise the wrapper parks and requires <code>ax resume</code>. On macOS,\n9934|Linux, and WSL2, tmux-resurrect/continuum MAY recreate panes but the wrapper\n9935|still performs these checks. Native Windows creates a new ConPTY and provider\n9936|process; it does not resurrect process memory.\n9937|\n9938|On macOS, logout or reboot without a newly verified GUI realm parks recovery\n9939|until GUI login. Background restore MAY contact an existing broker but MUST NOT\n9940|create the credential-dependent AX tmux server or infer provider authentication\n9941|from <code>launchctl managername</code> or a cached sentinel.\n9942|\n9943|### 13.12 Failure and recovery matrix\n9944|\n9945|| Failure | Required behavior | Recovery |\n9946|| --- | --- | --- |\n9947|| SSH disconnect during record/chunk transfer | Keep verified staging and immutable committed objects; no partial materialization | Retry <code>ax sync --resume TRANSFER_ID</code> |\n9948|| Invalid digest/schema | Quarantine object, stop affected sync, identify peer/object without payload logging | Repair source or remove peer authorization; fetch a known-good object |\n9949|| Workspace divergence | No destination write | Diff, copy, worktree, or explicit managed-replica replacement |\n9950|| Provider quiesce cannot prove full idle | Graceful stop/takeover fails; owner unchanged | Wait/retry or explicit force action |\n9951|| Provider exits but store handles remain open | No post-stop/superseding checkpoint or takeover lease | Wait boundedly, diagnose, or force with unclean marker |\n9952|| Destination disk full | Retain existing destination; staging can remain partial | Free space and resume |\n9953|| Atomic rename blocked | Roll back or retain staging; never in-place overwrite | Close handles and retry |\n9954|| Plugin crash/invalid stdout | Record provider-host error; do not infer capability or success | Run doctor, repair/upgrade plugin, retry |\n9955|| Epoch-1 launch fails before first checkpoint | Never report stopped/resumable or invent a checkpoint | Reconcile and retry the same bootstrap identity, establish the first checkpoint, or prove closure and record non-resumable bootstrap abort |\n9956|| Task-board bridge missing/incompatible | Do not inspect private state; task-board portability disabled | Install compatible task-board contract |\n9957|| Task-board import/open/adopt fails before new lease | Old owner remains authoritative in graceful flow | Roll back dormant import and retry |\n9958|| Task-board adopt fails after new lease | Destination remains stopped owner | Retry adopt/resume or newer explicit transfer |\n9959|| Owner-resume response is lost | Preserve prepared journal and do not start a second process/manager | Reconcile materialization plus provider/bridge status, then finalize, roll back pre-activation, or explicitly stop post-activation |\n9960|| Antigravity backend cannot resolve UUID | No fake resume or blank replacement | Authenticate correct realm, use provider-native fork if possible, or report unsupported |\n9961|| Muse cron/background state cannot be fenced | Portable takeover/fork unavailable | Stop locally or wait for a supported adapter/version |\n9962|| Concurrent force takeovers | Deterministic lease winner; preserve losing history | Stop losing process and reconcile divergent branch |\n9963|| Old owner reconnects after force | Reject its lower/losing fencing token from authoritative sync/resume | Park/stop stale process; inspect divergent events |\n9964|| SQLite index corrupt | Do not sync database | Move corrupt index to local diagnostics and rebuild from immutable truth |\n9965|| Operator interrupt | Preserve transaction journal and report whether authority changed | Retry same operation ID; inspect status before another takeover |\n9966|\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
