rappers; and\n9929|7. auto-resume only sessions whose configuration explicitly enables\n9930|   <code>restore.auto_resume</code> and whose provider safe-stop/restore gate\n9931|   passed.\n9932|\n9933|Otherwise the wrapper parks and requires <code>ax resume</code>. On macOS,\n9934|Linux, and WSL2, tmux-resurrect/continuum MAY recreate panes but the wrapper\n9935|still performs these checks. Native Windows creates a new ConPTY and provider\n9936|process; it does not resurrect process memory.\n9937|\n9938|On macOS, logout or reboot without a newly verified GUI realm parks recovery\n9939|until GUI login. Background restore MAY contact an existing broker but MUST NOT\n9940|create the credential-dependent AX tmux server or infer provider authentication\n9941|from <code>launchctl managername</code> or a cached sentinel.\n9942|\n9943|### 13.12 Failure and recovery matrix\n9944|\n9945|| Failure | Required behavior | Recovery |\n9946|| --- | --- | --- |\n9947|| SSH disconnect during record/chunk transfer | Keep verified staging and immutable committed objects; no partial materialization | Retry <code>ax sync --resume TRANSFER_ID</code> |\n9948|| Invalid digest/schema | Quarantine object, stop affected sync, identify peer/object without payload logging | Repair source or remove peer authorization; fetch a known-good object |\n9949|| Workspace divergence | No destination write | Diff, copy, worktree, or explicit managed-replica replacement |\n9950|| Provider quiesce cannot prove full idle | Graceful stop/takeover fails; owner unchanged | Wait/retry or explicit force action |\n9951|| Provider exits but store handles remain open | No post-stop/superseding checkpoint or takeover lease | Wait boundedly, diagnose, or force with unclean marker |\n9952|| Destination disk full | Retain existing destination; staging can remain partial | Free space and resume |\n9953|| Atomic rename blocked | Roll back or retain staging; never in-place overwrite | Close handles and retry |\n9954|| Plugin crash/invalid stdout | Record provider-host error; do not infer capability or success | Run doctor, repair/upgrade plugin, retry |\n9955|| Epoch-1 launch fails before first checkpoint | Never report stopped/resumable or invent a checkpoint | Reconcile and retry the same bootstrap identity, establish the first checkpoint, or prove closure and record non-resumable bootstrap abort |\n9956|| Task-board bridge missing/incompatible | Do not inspect private state; task-board portability disabled | Install compatible task-board contract |\n9957|| Task-board import/open/adopt fails before new lease | Old owner remains authoritative in graceful flow | Roll back dormant import and retry |\n9958|| Task-board adopt fails after new lease | Destination remains stopped owner | Retry adopt/resume or newer explicit transfer |\n9959|| Owner-resume response is lost | Preserve prepared journal and do not start a second process/manager | Reconcile materialization plus provider/bridge status, then finalize, roll back pre-activation, or explicitly stop post-activation |\n9960|| Antigravity backend cannot resolve UUID | No fake resume or blank replacement | Authenticate correct realm, use provider-native fork if possible, or report unsupported |\n9961|| Muse cron/background state cannot be fenced | Portable takeover/fork unavailable | Stop locally or wait for a supported adapter/version |\n9962|| Concurrent force takeovers | Deterministic lease winner; preserve losing history | Stop losing process and reconcile divergent branch |\n9963|| Old owner reconnects after force | Reject its lower/losing fencing token from authoritative sync/resume | Park/stop stale process; inspect divergent events |\n9964|| SQLite index corrupt | Do not sync database | Move corrupt index to local diagnostics and rebuild from immutable truth |\n9965|| Operator interrupt | Preserve transaction journal and report whether authority changed | Retry same operation ID; inspect status before another takeover |\n9966|\n(