{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cfd5","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b0ab-f92f-74d3-a245-61ad42401b4b"},"sequence":1605,"recorded_at":1780531400003205,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"8ab0c8df-167f-48db-b83c-f756aeede0a9","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"8ab0c8df-167f-48db-b83c-f756aeede0a9","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"8ab0c8df-167f-48db-b83c-f756aeede0a9"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b0ba-3267-7810-b1d0-fe4c9a2f9fb1"},"task_id":"01a0b0ba-3267-7810-b1d0-fe4c9a2f9fb1","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b0ba-3267-7810-b1d0-fe4c9a2f9fb1","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-26-1\",\n  \"command\": \"sed -n '275,330p' internal/axerror/details.go; echo ===; grep -n \\\"CapabilitiesForOperation\\\\|CheckOperation\\\" internal/terminalbackend/*_test.go | head -5; echo ===; grep -rn \\\"UnsignedEvidenceBytes\\\" internal/terminalbackend/*.go | grep -v _test | head -3\",\n  \"description\": \"Read realm evidence details and helpers\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"// caller_realm, broker_state, tmux_server_generation, and remediation\\\".\\n//\\n// tmux_server_generation is carried here on that clause's explicit instruction.\\n// The Section 16.2 exclusion of backend generations governs manifests and\\n// bundles generated by ax, and the more specific clause licenses this one\\n// diagnostic field.\\ntype RealmEvidence struct {\\n\\tCapability           string\\n\\tCallerRealm          string\\n\\tBrokerState          string\\n\\tTmuxServerGeneration string\\n\\tRemediation          string\\n}\\n\\n// Details renders the typed set. Every field is required, because a caller that\\n// omits one has not produced the typed details the clause names.\\nfunc (evidence RealmEvidence) Details() (Details, error) {\\n\\treturn requiredTypedDetails(map[string]string{\\n\\t\\t\\\"capability\\\":             evidence.Capability,\\n\\t\\t\\\"caller_realm\\\":           evidence.CallerRealm,\\n\\t\\t\\\"broker_state\\\":           evidence.BrokerState,\\n\\t\\t\\\"tmux_server_generation\\\": evidence.TmuxServerGeneration,\\n\\t\\t\\\"remediation\\\":            evidence.Remediation,\\n\\t})\\n}\\n\\n// TargetAuth is the exact typed detail set Section 15.3 requires for\\n// target_auth_missing: \\\"typed provider_id, provider_build, macos_version,\\n// tmux_server_generation, and remediation\\\".\\ntype TargetAuth struct {\\n\\tProviderID           string\\n\\tProviderBuild        string\\n\\tMacOSVersion         string\\n\\tTmuxServerGeneration string\\n\\tRemediation          string\\n}\\n\\n// Details renders the typed set. Every field is required.\\nfunc (target TargetAuth) Details() (Details, error) {\\n\\treturn requiredTypedDetails(map[string]string{\\n\\t\\t\\\"provider_id\\\":            target.ProviderID,\\n\\t\\t\\\"provider_build\\\":         target.ProviderBuild,\\n\\t\\t\\\"macos_version\\\":          target.MacOSVersion,\\n\\t\\t\\\"tmux_server_generation\\\": target.TmuxServerGeneration,\\n\\t\\t\\\"remediation\\\":            target.Remediation,\\n\\t})\\n}\\n\\n// targetAuthMissingKeys is the presence requirement New enforces for\\n// target_auth_missing, so the generic constructor cannot emit that code with a\\n// weaker detail set than the typed constructor produces.\\nvar targetAuthMissingKeys = []string{\\n\\t\\\"macos_version\\\",\\n\\t\\\"provider_build\\\",\\n\\t\\\"provider_id\\\",\\n\\t\\\"remediation\\\",\\n===\\ninternal/terminalbackend/backend_id_entry_census_test.go:276:\\t{entry: \\\"CapabilitiesForOperation\\\", reason: \\\"static capability table lookup; its refusals name operations only\\\"},\\ninternal/terminalbackend/backend_id_entry_census_test.go:277:\\t{entry: \\\"CheckOperation\\\", reason: \\\"operates on admitted capabilities; its refusals name operations only\\\"},\\ninternal/terminalbackend/manifest_pin_test.go:142:\\tbeforeCreate, err := CapabilitiesForOperation(\\\"create\\\")\\ninternal/terminalbackend/manifest_pin_test.go:144:\\t\\tt.Fatalf(\\\"CapabilitiesForOperation(create) error = %v\\\", err)\\ninternal/terminalbackend/manifest_pin_test.go:169:\\tafterCreate, err := CapabilitiesForOperation(\\\"create\\\")\\n===\\ninternal/terminalbackend/manifest.go:1505:// UnsignedEvidenceBytes, and signature the decoded attestation bytes. A nil\\ninternal/terminalbackend/manifest.go:1522:// UnsignedEvidenceBytes rebuilds the exact bytes an attestation signs: ASCII\\ninternal/terminalbackend/manifest.go:1527:func UnsignedEvidenceBytes(evidence Evidence) ([]byte, error) {\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 3144,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 786,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cfd7","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b0ab-f92f-74d3-a245-61ad42401b4b"},"sequence":1606,"recorded_at":1780531400003207,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"8ab0c8df-167f-48db-b83c-f756aeede0a9","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"8ab0c8df-167f-48db-b83c-f756aeede0a9","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"8ab0c8df-167f-48db-b83c-f756aeede0a9"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b0ba-3267-7810-b1d0-fe4c9a2f9fb1"},"task_id":"01a0b0ba-3267-7810-b1d0-fe4c9a2f9fb1","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"01a0b0ba-3267-7810-b1d0-fe4c9a2f9fb1"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cfd9","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b0ab-f92f-74d3-a245-61ad42401b4b"},"sequence":1607,"recorded_at":1780531400003209,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"8ab0c8df-167f-48db-b83c-f756aeede0a9","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"8ab0c8df-167f-48db-b83c-f756aeede0a9","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"8ab0c8df-167f-48db-b83c-f756aeede0a9"},"call_id":"call_01a0b0ba277e77fc9055d4503998deb6","text":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(1353 line(s) above)\n1354|### 4.1 Terminal backend interface\n1355|\n1356|Every terminal backend MUST implement these semantic operations:\n1357|\n1358|| Operation | Required result |\n1359|| --- | --- |\n1360|| <code>create</code> | With <code>session_id</code> and caller-stable <code>bootstrap_operation_id</code>, create a durable pane/process whose only stable entry point is <code>ax pane SESSION_ID</code>. |\n1361|| <code>attach</code> | Connect an operator to the local terminal without changing ownership. |\n1362|| <code>status</code> | Report process presence, wrapper state, provider child state, and attachability. |\n1363|| <code>quiesce-input</code> | Stop new operator/provider input while retaining observation. |\n1364|| <code>wait-safe-boundary</code> | Prove the adapter-specific safe boundary or time out. |\n1365|| <code>request-stop</code> | Ask the provider to exit through a version-tested graceful path. |\n1366|| <code>terminate-stale</code> | Terminate a process only for explicit force recovery after preserving diagnostics. |\n1367|| <code>restore</code> | Recreate the wrapper after reboot and consult current ownership before any provider resume. |\n1368|\n1369|The wrapper MUST validate configuration, load the logical session, synchronize\n1370|known lease records when possible, and compare the local fencing token before\n1371|launching a provider. It MUST park safely when ownership is remote, ambiguous,\n1372|or unverified.\n1373|\n1374|Terminal creation and the wrapper's first child start are idempotent on\n1375|<code>(session_id, bootstrap_operation_id)</code>. The backend MUST durably bind\n1376|that pair before child creation. An identical retry returns or reattaches to\n1377|the one recorded wrapper/child; changing the operation for a session still in\n1378|the bootstrap window is <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>. After a lost result,\n1379|<code>status</code> plus that binding MUST prove absence or identify the one\n1380|child before any start retry. This contract never persists or replicates a PID\n1381|as identity.\n1382|\n1383|### 4.2 tmux backend\n1384|\n1385|On macOS, Linux, and WSL2, the supported durable terminal backend is tmux. Every\n1386|managed pane MUST run:\n1387|\n1388|~~~shell\n1389|ax pane <logical-session-id>\n1390|~~~\n1391|\n1392|It MUST NOT run the raw provider command as the pane's stable command.\n1393|<code>tmux-resurrect</code> plus <code>tmux-continuum</code> MAY recreate local\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
